cite_internationale_des_arts_faaa6d16811c,cite_internationale_des_arts,https://www.hkst.de/en/scholarships_/applications-2/,https://bewerberportal.hkst.de/teamworks.dll?ShowSysMessages=true&urlencUTF8=true,Hessische Kulturstiftung,en,Hessische Kulturstiftung 2027/2028 travel and residency grants,"Visual artists who … were born in Hesse or have lived in Hesse (primary residence) since no later than 1 January 2025 or have completed a degree at an art academy or a comparable course of study/training in Hesse can apply. There is no age limit. Artist duos may submit a joint application. Applications are not accepted from persons who … have been awarded a Hessische Kulturstiftung travel or residency grant in the past (does not apply to State of Hesse work, project, or gap grants) are still in the process of pursuing a degree vocational training programme at the time of the application are related to one of the jury members, are employed by the Hessische Kulturstiftung, or are related to a Hessische Kulturstiftung employee.",Hessische Kulturstiftung 2027/2028 travel and residency grants,"Visual artists who … were born in Hesse or have lived in Hesse (primary residence) since no later than 1 January 2025 or have completed a degree at an art academy or a comparable course of study/training in Hesse can apply. There is no age limit. Artist duos may submit a joint application. Applications are not accepted from persons who … have been awarded a Hessische Kulturstiftung travel or residency grant in the past (does not apply to State of Hesse work, project, or gap grants) are still in the process of pursuing a degree vocational training programme at the time of the application are related to one of the jury members, are employed by the Hessische Kulturstiftung, or are related to a Hessische Kulturstiftung employee.",15 October 2026,2026-10-15,2026-09-23 07:57:22.409903+00:00
culture_gouv_fr_1pct_3466233e56ff,culture_gouv_fr_1pct,https://www.culture.gouv.fr/regions/drac-hauts-de-france/appel-a-candidatures-1-artistique-du-ministere-de-la-justice-unite-judiciaire-a-priorite-educative-ujpe-de-liancourt-60,https://www.marches-publics.gouv.fr/app.php/entreprise/consultation/3064004?orgAcronyme=d3f,DRAC Hauts-de-France / Ministère de la Culture,fr,appel à candidatures 1% artistique du ministère de la justice - unité judiciaire à priorité éducative (UJPE) de Liancourt (60),"témogn[e] d’une expérience artistique compatible avec les missions éducatives, sociales et organisationnelles de l’UJPE de Liancourt, articulées à une temporalité ritualisée et à la construction d’un projet d’insertion individualisé. Les notions de parcours, d’évolutions, de perspectives et de possibles y sont importantes .",Call for applications 1% artistic of the Ministry of Justice - educational priority judicial unit (UJPE) of Liancourt (60),"Demonstrate artistic experience compatible with the educational, social and organizational missions of the UJPE of Liancourt, articulated around a ritualized temporality and the construction of an individualized integration project. The notions of pathway, developments, perspectives and possibilities are important there.",12 octobre 2026 à 12h,2026-09-23,2026-09-23 07:57:23.441370+00:00
culture_gouv_fr_1pct_c2e74aeae78d,culture_gouv_fr_1pct,https://www.culture.gouv.fr/catalogue-des-demarches-et-subventions/appels-a-projet-partenaires/appel-a-candidatures-pour-le-1-artistique-dans-le-cadre-de-la-construction-du-nouveau-college-de-groisy-en-haute-savoie-74,https://hautesavoie.fr/le-departement/marches-publics/,Ministère de la Culture / Département de la Haute-Savoie,fr,Appel à candidatures pour le 1% artistique dans le cadre de la construction du nouveau collège de Groisy en Haute-Savoie (74),"Cet appel à projet s'adresse aux artistes ou groupements d'artistes. Il est interdit à un même candidat, quelle que soit la compétence, de se présenter en qualité : de candidat individuel et de membre de plusieurs groupements, de membre de plusieurs groupements.",Call for applications for the 1% artistic scheme as part of the construction of the new middle school in Groisy in Haute-Savoie (74),"This call for projects is addressed to artists or groups of artists. A single candidate, regardless of expertise, is not permitted to apply in the capacity of: an individual candidate and a member of several groups, or a member of several groups.",19 octobre 2026,2026-10-19,2026-09-23 07:57:24.571463+00:00
culture_gouv_fr_1pct_c98d49e01733,culture_gouv_fr_1pct,https://www.culture.gouv.fr/catalogue-des-demarches-et-subventions/appels-a-projet-partenaires/1-artistique-a-issy-les-moulineaux.-une-aeuvre-a-imaginer-pour-le-futur-groupe-scolaire-des-epinettes,https://marches.maximilien.fr/,Ville d'Issy-les-Moulineaux / Grand Paris Seine Ouest (GPSO),fr,1% artistique à Issy-les-Moulineaux. Une œuvre à imaginer pour le futur groupe scolaire des Épinettes,"Cet appel à candidatures s'adresse aux artistes professionnels relevant des arts visuels et plastiques. Les candidatures peuvent être présentées à titre individuel ou sous la forme d'un groupement, le mandataire devant obligatoirement être un artiste.",1% artistic in Issy-les-Moulineaux. A work to be imagined for the future Épinettes school group,"This call for applications is addressed to professional artists working in the visual and plastic arts. Applications may be submitted individually or as a group, with the lead applicant required to be an artist.",5 octobre 2026 à 17 heures,2026-01-17,2026-09-23 07:57:25.852506+00:00
dgartes_portugal_d62fab0a8e9d,dgartes_portugal,http://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/aviso_abertura_apoio_sustentado_27_30_programacao.pdf,,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),pt,Programa de Apoio Sustentado às Artes – Programação,"1. Pessoas coletivas de direito privado com sede em Portugal, que aqui exerçam a título predominante atividades profissionais numa ou mais das áreas artísticas previstas no artigo 1.º, n.º 2 do Decreto -Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual, de acordo com as seguintes condições de acesso:   
a) Modalidade de apoio Bienal: tenham, pelo menos, quatro anos de atividade profissional continuada; 
b) Modalidade de apoio Quadrienal: tenham, pelo menos, seis anos de atividade profissional continuada;  ter beneficiado, pelo menos uma vez nos últimos seis anos, de apoio financeiro do Estado através da DGARTES na tipologia de apoio sustentado, desde que não lhes tenha sido aplicada a sanção prevista na alínea c) do n.º 1 do artigo 23.º, nem se encontre em aplicação a sanção prevista na alínea a) do n.º 1 do mesmo artigo, independentemente da sua natureza jurídica ou do seu modelo institucional; dispor de espaço de criação e/ou de apresentação adequado à prossecução da atividade apoiada.

2. Para efeitos de acesso à modalidade prevista na alínea b) do n.º 1, consideram -se os dois últimos ciclos de apoio sustentado (2018-2022 e 2023 -2026), na modalidade quadrienal e bienal, atribuído ao abrigo do Decreto-Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual.
3. Não são admitidas ao procedimento concursal as fundações privadas ou as fundações públicas de direito privado que tenham outro tipo de financiamento continuado,  assegurado pelo programa orçamental da área da cultura, bem como as associações  maioritariamente constituídas por entidades públicas e as empresas do setor empresarial do Estado e das regiões autónomas.
4. Não são admitidas ao proc edimento concursal as entidades que tenham assinado adenda de renovação do contrato do apoio sustentado na modalidade quadrienal.
5. As entidades devem enquadrar a sua atividade em apenas uma candidatura e, em caso de concessão de apoio, o respetivo contrato constitui o único instrumento de apoio para o período a que se destina, salvo o disposto no n.º 4 do artigo 26.º do Decreto-Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual.",Sustained Arts Support Programme – Programming,"1. Private legal persons with headquarters in Portugal, who predominantly carry out professional activities here in one or more of the artistic areas provided for in article 1(2) of Decree-Law No. 103/2017 of 24 August, in its current wording, in accordance with the following access conditions:
   a) Biennial support modality: have at least four years of continuous professional activity;
   b) Quadrennial support modality: have at least six years of continuous professional activity; have benefited at least once in the last six years from financial support from the State through DGARTES under the sustained support type, provided that the sanction provided for in point c) of paragraph 1 of article 23 has not been applied to them, nor is the sanction provided for in point a) of paragraph 1 of the same article in effect, regardless of their legal nature or institutional model; have a creation and/or presentation space suitable for carrying out the supported activity.

2. For the purposes of access to the modality provided for in paragraph b) of paragraph 1, the last two sustained support cycles (2018-2022 and 2023-2026), in the quadrennial and biennial modality, awarded under Decree-Law No. 103/2017 of 24 August, in its current wording, are considered.
3. Private foundations or public foundations governed by private law that have other types of continuing funding, ensured by the budget programme of the culture area, as well as associations mainly made up of public entities and companies in the State business sector and of the autonomous regions, are not admitted to the tender procedure.
4. Entities that have signed an addendum renewing the sustained support contract in the quadrennial modality are not admitted to the tender procedure.
5. Entities must frame their activity in only one application and, in the event that support is granted, the respective contract constitutes the only support instrument for the period to which it is intended, except as provided for in article 26(4) of Decree-Law No. 103/2017 of 24 August, in its current wording.",Conforme aviso publicado na 2.ª série do Diário da República de 24 de agosto,2027-08-24,2026-09-23 07:57:29.007574+00:00
dgartes_portugal_5d8f41b87131,dgartes_portugal,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/pt/apoio/10177,https://apoios.dgartes.gov.pt/,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),pt,PROGRAMA DE APOIO SUSTENTADO ÀS ARTES — PROGRAMAÇÃO,No page text provided beyond the call announcement and deadline; specific eligibility/restriction criteria are not stated in the given text.,Sustained Support Programme for the Arts — Programming,No page text provided beyond the call announcement and deadline; specific eligibility/restriction criteria are not stated in the given text.,a apresentação das candidaturas termina às 17h59m59s do dia 6 de outubro de 2026,2026-09-24,2026-09-23 07:57:29.889519+00:00
dgartes_portugal_dd8e96231487,dgartes_portugal,http://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/aviso_abertura_apoio_sustentado_27_30_teatro.pdf,,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),pt,"PROGRAMA DE APOIO SUSTENTADO ÀS ARTES TEATRO (CRIAÇÃO, EDIÇÃO, FORMAÇÃO, AÇÕES ESTRATÉGICAS DE MEDIAÇÃO)","1. Pessoas coletivas de direito privado com sede em Portugal, que aqui exerçam a título predominante atividades profissionais numa ou mais das áreas artísticas previstas no artigo 1.º, n.º 2 do Decreto -Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual, de acordo com as seguintes condições de acesso: 
a) Modalidade de apoio Bienal: tenham, pelo menos, quatro anos de atividade profissional continuada; 
b) Modalidade de apoio Quadrienal: tenham, pelo menos, seis anos de atividade profissional continuada;  ter beneficiado, pelo menos uma vez nos últimos seis anos, de apoio financeiro do Estado através da DGARTES na tipologia de apoio   
sustentado, desde que não lhes tenha sido aplicada a sanção prevista na alínea c) 
do n.º 1 do artigo 23.º, nem se encontre em aplicação a sanção prevista na alínea 
a) do n.º 1 do mesmo artigo, independentemente da sua natureza jurídica ou do seu 
modelo institucional; dispor de espaço de criação e/ou de apresentação adequado 
à prossecução da atividade apoiada.

2. Para efeitos de acesso à modalidade prevista na alínea b) do n.º 1, consideram -se os 
dois últimos ciclos de apoio sustentado (2018-2022 e 2023 -2026), na modalidade 
quadrienal e bienal, atribuído ao abrigo do Decreto-Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, 
na redação atual.
3. Não são admitidas ao procedimento concursal as fundações privadas ou as fundações 
públicas de direito privado que tenham outro tipo de financiamento continuado,  
assegurado pelo programa orçamental da área da cultura, bem como as associações  
maioritariamente constituídas por entidades públicas e as empresas do setor 
empresarial do Estado e das regiões autónomas.
4. Não são admitidas ao proc edimento concursal as entidades que tenham assinado 
adenda de renovação do contrato do apoio sustentado na modalidade quadrienal.
5. As entidades devem enquadrar a sua atividade em apenas uma candidatura e, em caso 
de concessão de apoio, o respetivo contrato constitui o único instrumento de apoio 
para o período a que se destina, salvo o disposto no n.º 4 do artigo 26.º do Decreto-Lei 
n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual.","SUSTAINED SUPPORT PROGRAMME FOR THE ARTS THEATRE (CREATION, PUBLISHING, TRAINING, STRATEGIC MEDIATION ACTIONS)","1. Private-law legal persons with headquarters in Portugal, which carry out, on a predominant basis, professional activities in one or more of the artistic areas provided for in Article 1(2) of Decree-Law No. 103/2017, of 24 August, in its current wording, according to the following access conditions:
a) Biennial support modality: have at least four years of continuous professional activity;
b) Quadriennial support modality: have at least six years of continuous professional activity; have benefited, at least once in the last six years, from financial support from the State through DGARTES under the sustained support typology, provided that the sanction provided for in point (c) of paragraph 1 of Article 23 has not been applied to them, nor is the sanction provided for in point (a) of paragraph 1 of the same article being applied, regardless of their legal nature or institutional model; have a creation and/or presentation space suitable for the pursuit of the supported activity.

2. For the purposes of access to the modality provided for in point b) of paragraph 1, the last two cycles of sustained support (2018-2022 and 2023-2026), in the quadriennial and biennial modalities, granted under Decree-Law No. 103/2017, of 24 August, in its current wording, shall be considered.
3. Private foundations or public foundations under private law that have other types of continuous funding, ensured by the budget programme for the culture area, as well as associations made up mostly of public entities and companies in the State business sector and in the autonomous regions, are not admitted to the tender procedure.
4. Entities that have signed an addendum renewing the sustained support contract in the quadriennial modality are not admitted to the tender procedure.
5. Entities must frame their activity in only one application and, in the event of support being granted, the respective contract constitutes the sole support instrument for the period to which it is intended, save as provided for in paragraph 4 of Article 26 of Decree-Law No. 103/2017, of 24 August, in its current wording.",,,2026-09-23 07:57:33.237488+00:00
