dgartes_portugal_560664dc6138,dgartes_portugal,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/pt/apoio/10172,https://apoios.dgartes.gov.pt/,DGARTES,pt,"PROGRAMA DE APOIO SUSTENTADO ÀS ARTES — ARTES VISUAIS (CRIAÇÃO, PROGRAMAÇÃO, EDIÇÃO, FORMAÇÃO, AÇÕES ESTRATÉGICAS DE MEDIAÇÃO)","A Direção-Geral das Artes torna pública, através do Aviso n.º 20875-B/2026/2 , a abertura do concurso para a apresentação de candidaturas no âmbito do Programa de Apoio Sustentado na área das Artes Visuais, conforme o disposto no Decreto-Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual, e no Regulamento dos Programas de Apoio às Artes, aprovado em anexo à Portaria n.º 345-A/2026/1, de 14 de agosto.","SUSTAINED SUPPORT PROGRAM FOR THE ARTS — VISUAL ARTS (CREATION, PROGRAMMING, PUBLISHING, TRAINING, STRATEGIC MEDIATION ACTIONS)","The Directorate-General for the Arts hereby makes public, through Notice No. 20875-B/2026/2, the opening of the competition for the submission of applications within the scope of the Sustained Support Program in the area of Visual Arts, pursuant to Decree-Law No. 103/2017, of 24 August, in its current wording, and the Regulations for the Arts Support Programs, approved in an annex to Ordinance No. 345-A/2026/1, of 14 August.",a apresentação das candidaturas termina às 17h59m59s do dia 6 de outubro de 2026,2026-09-24,2026-09-23 07:57:51.596129+00:00
dgartes_portugal_9958967f7dcb,dgartes_portugal,http://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/avisodeabertura_bv2027.pdf,,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),pt,Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"E. Destinatários: Nos termos do Aviso n.º 15360/2026/2, de 22 de junho, foram selecionadas as seguintes propostas a convidar para integrar o concurso limitado:
− Analog Twins, de Alice Clanet-Hallard, Edgar Brito, Francisco Lobo e Romea Muryn
− Mãos ao Chão (Hands to the Ground), de Joanna Alice Helm, Remígio Van Eyes Chilaule
e Samuel de Brito Gonçalves
− Matéria Viva — Os materiais da construção portuguesa e o saber que resiste, de Helena
Botelho

H. Objetivos de interesse público cultural:

Objetivos estratégicos: as entidades candidatas devem, obrigatoriamente, evidenciar a
correspondência a, pelo menos, um dos objetivos abaixo indicados.
1. Fomentar, valorizar e promover a arquitetura, nas suas diversas manifestações, as suas
interseções e diálogos transversais com outras disciplinas artísticas e áreas do conhecimento e
a inclusão de linguagens de interação, mediação e comunicação através do recurso a meios
digitais e eletrónicos;
2. Enquadrar conceptualmente a candidatura no tema proposto pelos curadores da Bienal de
Arquitetura 2027, Wang Shu e Lu Wenyu (DO ARCHITECTURE — FOR THE POSSIBILITY OF
COEXISTENCE FACING A REAL REALITY).

Objetivos específicos de interesse público cultural: as entidades candidatas devem, obrigatoriamente,
evidenciar a correspondência a dois dos objetivos abaixo indicados .

1. Dinamizar a internacionalização das artes e da cultura portuguesa através da cooperação com
outros países;
2. Valorizar a dimensão educativa e da sensibilização para a cultura através de boas práticas de
mediação de públicos;
3. Valorizar a pesquisa e experimentação artísticas como práticas inovadoras do desenvolvimento
e do conhecimento;
4. Fomentar a sustentabilidade ambiental e a implementação de boas práticas ecológicas;
5. Promover a acessibilidade física, social e intelectual de todos os profissionais envolvidos nos
projetos artísticos e dos respetivos públicos.",Support Programme for Projects – Official Portuguese Representation at the 20th International Architecture Exhibition – La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"E. Recipients: Under Notice No. 15360/2026/2, of 22 June, the following proposals were selected to be invited to join the restricted competition:
− Analog Twins, by Alice Clanet-Hallard, Edgar Brito, Francisco Lobo and Romea Muryn
− Mãos ao Chão (Hands to the Ground), by Joanna Alice Helm, Remígio Van Eyes Chilaule
and Samuel de Brito Gonçalves
− Matéria Viva — Os materiais da construção portuguesa e o saber que resiste, by Helena
Botelho

H. Public cultural interest objectives:

Strategic objectives: applicant entities must, obligatorily, demonstrate that they correspond to at least one of the objectives indicated below.
1. Foster, enhance and promote architecture, in its various manifestations, its intersections and cross-cutting dialogues with other artistic disciplines and areas of knowledge, and the inclusion of languages of interaction, mediation and communication through the use of digital and electronic means;
2. Conceptually frame the application within the theme proposed by the curators of the 2027 Architecture Biennale, Wang Shu and Lu Wenyu (DO ARCHITECTURE — FOR THE POSSIBILITY OF COEXISTENCE FACING A REAL REALITY).

Specific objectives of public cultural interest: applicant entities must, obligatorily, demonstrate that they correspond to two of the objectives indicated below.

1. Boost the internationalization of Portuguese arts and culture through cooperation with other countries;
2. Enhance the educational dimension and awareness-raising for culture through good practices in audience mediation;
3. Value artistic research and experimentation as innovative practices of development and knowledge;
4. Foster environmental sustainability and the implementation of good ecological practices;
5. Promote the physical, social and intellectual accessibility of all professionals involved in the artistic projects and of their respective audiences.",6 de outubro de 2026,2026-10-06,2026-09-23 07:57:54.193624+00:00
dgartes_portugal_c966cce2ccf0,dgartes_portugal,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/pt/apoio/10166,https://apoios.dgartes.gov.pt/,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),pt,[Concurso Limitado] Programa de Apoio a Projetos - Representação Oficial Portuguesa na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura - La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"conforme o disposto no Decreto-Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual e no Regulamento dos Programas de Apoio às Artes aprovado em anexo à Portaria n.º 345-A/2026/1, de 14 de agosto.",[Limited Competition] Project Support Program - Official Portuguese Representation at the 20th International Architecture Exhibition - La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"as provided for in Decree-Law No. 103/2017, of 24 August, in its current wording, and in the Regulations for the Arts Support Programs approved in annex to Ordinance No. 345-A/2026/1, of 14 August.",a apresentação de candidaturas termina às 17h59m59s do dia 6 de outubro de 2026,2026-09-24,2026-09-23 07:57:55.207475+00:00
dgartes_portugal_b0e4ca961b8e,dgartes_portugal,http://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/aviso_abertura_orquestra_regional_alentejo_2026.pdf,,DGARTES,pt,Concurso para criação de Orquestra Regional do Alentejo,"Pessoas coletivas de direito privado sem fins lucrativos, com sede na região do Alentejo , doravante designadas entidades promotoras das orquestras regionais.
Não são admitidas ao procedimento concursal as fundações privadas ou as fundações públicas de direito privado que tenham outro tipo de financiamento continuado, assegurado pelo programa orçamental da área da cultura, bem como empresas do setor público empresarial do Estado.
2. Estão impedidas de apresentar candidaturas ao presente programa de apoio  as entidades beneficiárias de Apoio Sustentado.   

3. Os órgãos sociais das entidades promotoras das orquestras regionais devem incluir  um número mínimo de cinco municípios na circunscrição territorial ( NUTS II) do Alentejo.
4. Os órgãos sociais podem incluir ainda outros agentes locais ou regionais da região onde se insere a Orquestra Regional, para além do número de municípios mencionados no n.º 3.",Call for the creation of the Alentejo Regional Orchestra,"Private legal entities without profit-making purposes, headquartered in the Alentejo region, hereinafter designated promoters of the regional orchestras.
Private foundations or public foundations governed by private law that have another type of ongoing funding, secured by the budget program of the culture area, as well as companies in the State public business sector, are not admitted to the tender procedure.
2. Entities benefiting from Sustained Support are barred from submitting applications to this support program.

3. The governing bodies of the promoters of the regional orchestras must include a minimum number of five municipalities in the territorial constituency (NUTS II) of Alentejo.
4. The governing bodies may also include other local or regional agents from the region where the Regional Orchestra is located, in addition to the number of municipalities mentioned in paragraph 3.",,,2026-09-23 07:57:56.856815+00:00
dgartes_portugal_cc9be82e728f,dgartes_portugal,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/pt/apoio/10064,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/formulario_concurso_orquestra_regional_alentejo_2026.xlsx,DGARTES,pt,CONCURSO PARA CRIAÇÃO DA ORQUESTRA REGIONAL DO ALENTEJO,Conforme aviso publicado na 2.ª série do Diário da República de 15 de julho,Competition for the Creation of the Alentejo Regional Orchestra,As stated in the notice published in the 2nd series of the Diário da República on 15 July,Novo prazo: a apresentação de candidaturas termina às 17:59:59 do dia 25 de setembro de 2026.,2026-09-23,2026-09-23 07:57:58.247529+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_ad15a329abd7,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-open-call-for-collaboration-grants/second-culture-helps-solidarity-call-for-collaboration-grants/,https://culture-of-solidarity-fund.grantplatform.com/,Culture Helps Solidarity,en,Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Collaboration Grants,"This call supports international projects that use arts and culture to aid the integration of displaced Ukrainians into host communities, with a strong focus on mental well-being, vulnerable groups, and veterans. The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country. Grants of up to €20,000 are available for partnerships of two organisations, and up to €30,000 for partnerships involving three or more partners. The projects should foster intercultural dialogue, professional exchange, and long-term solidarity.",Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Collaboration Grants,"This call supports international projects that use arts and culture to aid the integration of displaced Ukrainians into host communities, with a strong focus on mental well-being, vulnerable groups, and veterans. The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country. Grants of up to €20,000 are available for partnerships of two organisations, and up to €30,000 for partnerships involving three or more partners. The projects should foster intercultural dialogue, professional exchange, and long-term solidarity.","November 10, 2026, at 13:00 Amsterdam time / 14:00 Kyiv time",2026-11-10,2026-09-23 07:57:58.259152+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_f1e9b1c26c84,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/second-culture-helps-solidarity-call-for-project-grants/,https://culture-of-solidarity-fund.grantplatform.com/,Cultural Foundation,en,Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Project Grants,"We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice.",Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Project Grants,"We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice.",,,2026-09-23 07:57:58.259187+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_80ce5461aa91,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/new-fellowship-programme-to-research-the-ecf-historical-archives/,https://ecf-fellowship.grantplatform.com/,European Cultural Foundation,en,New Fellowship Programme to Research the ECF Historical Archives,"Fellows are expected to work substantially with the ECF archival holdings – primarily in English, with significant material in French, German, and Dutch, and additional languages occasionally represented.",New Fellowship Programme to Research the ECF Historical Archives,"Fellows are expected to work substantially with the ECF archival holdings – primarily in English, with significant material in French, German, and Dutch, and additional languages occasionally represented.",30 September 2026 at 17:00 CET.,2026-09-30,2026-09-23 07:57:58.266906+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_a246059c820a,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-open-call-for-individual-grants-4th-round/,https://qr1.be/8KS5J3,European Cultural Foundation,en,Culture Helps Solidarity: Open Call for Individual Grants (4th Round),"The programme offers flexible grants of up to €1,200 to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries.",Culture Helps Solidarity: Open Call for Individual Grants (4th Round),"The programme offers flexible grants of up to €1,200 to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries.",29 June 2026,2026-06-29,2026-09-23 07:57:58.270642+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_b0dabdcbc160,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-open-call-for-collaboration-grants-2/,,European Cultural Foundation,en,Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Collaboration Grants,"The call supports cultural projects that improve access to culture and foster inclusion and mental well-being for internally displaced people and refugees from Ukraine, with particular attention to vulnerable groups, including veterans. Priority is given to partnerships led by Ukrainian organisations, whether based in Ukraine or working in exile, especially when collaborating with organisations in neighbouring Creative Europe countries.",Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Collaboration Grants,"The call supports cultural projects that improve access to culture and foster inclusion and mental well-being for internally displaced people and refugees from Ukraine, with particular attention to vulnerable groups, including veterans. Priority is given to partnerships led by Ukrainian organisations, whether based in Ukraine or working in exile, especially when collaborating with organisations in neighbouring Creative Europe countries.",31 March 2026 at 13:00 Amsterdam time,2026-03-31,2026-09-23 07:57:58.275831+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_3b772a92765f,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-%d1%81%d0%be%d0%bb%d1%96%d0%b4%d0%b0%d1%80%d0%bd%d1%96%d1%81%d1%82-2/,https://culturalfoundation.eu/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/CH-S_Call-for-Proposals_No-1_Project-Grants_ENG.pdf,Cultural Foundation,en,"Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність Project Grants, round one","This first round of Project Calls supports cultural and artistic initiatives that respond to the changing landscape of community (dis‑)connection. We invite projects that help people navigate the social and emotional complexities of displacement, transition, and return by creating meaningful encounters, enabling shared cultural participation, and fostering renewed forms of solidarity. Through creativity and empathy, artistic processes can help communities move beyond immediate limitations while also acknowledging the ethical and emotional boundaries of cultural work.","Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність Project Grants, round one","This first round of Project Calls supports cultural and artistic initiatives that respond to the changing landscape of community (dis‑)connection. We invite projects that help people navigate the social and emotional complexities of displacement, transition, and return by creating meaningful encounters, enabling shared cultural participation, and fostering renewed forms of solidarity. Through creativity and empathy, artistic processes can help communities move beyond immediate limitations while also acknowledging the ethical and emotional boundaries of cultural work.","Thursday, 16th April 2026, 13:00 Amsterdam time/ 14:00 Kyiv time.",2026-04-16,2026-09-23 07:57:58.288100+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_67a05c59b453,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-open-call-for-individual-care-grants-round-2/,https://qr1.be/BXQZDY,European Cultural Foundation,en,Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Individual Care Grants Round 2,"The call supports Ukrainian cultural workers who need time and resources to focus on well-being, recovery and the conditions needed to continue their cultural work. The grants are open to artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals from Ukraine, whether they remain in the country or are temporarily displaced elsewhere.",Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Individual Care Grants Round 2,"The call supports Ukrainian cultural workers who need time and resources to focus on well-being, recovery and the conditions needed to continue their cultural work. The grants are open to artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals from Ukraine, whether they remain in the country or are temporarily displaced elsewhere.",6 April 2026 at 13:00 (Amsterdam time),2026-04-06,2026-09-23 07:57:58.292609+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_cf66f32bd199,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-%d1%81%d0%be%d0%bb%d1%96%d0%b4%d0%b0%d1%80%d0%bd%d1%96%d1%81%d1%82/,https://qr1.be/93Y8G0,European Cultural Foundation,en,Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність Individual Care Grants,"Grants of up to €1,200 are available to individuals working in arts and culture who support displaced Ukrainians, particularly vulnerable groups such as veterans, and who have themselves been affected by war or displacement.",Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність Individual Care Grants,"Grants of up to €1,200 are available to individuals working in arts and culture who support displaced Ukrainians, particularly vulnerable groups such as veterans, and who have themselves been affected by war or displacement.",from 2 to 23 February 2026,2026-02-23,2026-09-23 07:57:58.297196+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_6e02c5a9b950,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-open-call-for-collaboration-grants/,https://qr1.be/I99PBS,European Cultural Foundation,en,Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Collaboration Grants,"The call supports cultural projects that improve access to culture and foster inclusion and mental well-being for internally displaced people and refugees from Ukraine, with particular attention to vulnerable groups, including veterans. Priority is given to partnerships led by Ukrainian organisations, whether based in Ukraine or working in exile, especially when collaborating with organisations in neighbouring Creative Europe countries.",Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Collaboration Grants,"The call supports cultural projects that improve access to culture and foster inclusion and mental well-being for internally displaced people and refugees from Ukraine, with particular attention to vulnerable groups, including veterans. Priority is given to partnerships led by Ukrainian organisations, whether based in Ukraine or working in exile, especially when collaborating with organisations in neighbouring Creative Europe countries.",31 March 2026 at 13:00 Amsterdam time,2026-03-31,2026-09-23 07:57:58.301902+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_7395e3ac9c32,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/civitates-media-open-call/,https://civitates-eu.org/funding-opportunity/call-for-proposals-strengthening-independent-public-interest-journalism-in-europe/,Civitates,en,Civitates Media Open Call,"Civitates invites applications from independent media outlets registered in Hungary, Poland, Italy, Spain, Bulgaria, Slovakia, and Croatia.",Civitates Media Open Call,"Civitates invites applications from independent media outlets registered in Hungary, Poland, Italy, Spain, Bulgaria, Slovakia, and Croatia.",,,2026-09-23 07:57:58.332054+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_d1262c97a543,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-of-solidarity-fund/,,European Cultural Foundation,en,Culture of Solidarity Fund 2020 - 2024,"Through regular open calls, CoS supports cross-border collaboration between civil society and cultural organisations. The process is kept simple and accessible, with space for peer exchange and networking. Our upcoming open calls are due to launch in January 2026 and will have special focus on Ukrainian creative professionals and their European peers fostering social engagement, integration, and cohesion among displaced Ukrainians.",Culture of Solidarity Fund 2020 - 2024,"Through regular open calls, CoS supports cross-border collaboration between civil society and cultural organisations. The process is kept simple and accessible, with space for peer exchange and networking. Our upcoming open calls are due to launch in January 2026 and will have special focus on Ukrainian creative professionals and their European peers fostering social engagement, integration, and cohesion among displaced Ukrainians.",January 2026,2026-01-23,2026-09-23 07:57:58.351318+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_93665283fd01,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/the-europe-challenge-2022/,https://culturalfoundation.eu/stories/the-europe-challenge-application-and-criteria/,Cultural Foundation,en,The Europe Challenge 2022,"We are calling on every library in Europe to apply to the 2022 Europe Challenge: from public libraries to mobile, rural, school, university and prison libraries, municipal and national libraries. Every library in Europe is eligible to take part in the Europe Challenge, from public libraries to mobile, rural, school, university, and prison libraries, municipal and national libraries.",The Europe Challenge 2022,"We are calling on every library in Europe to apply to the 2022 Europe Challenge: from public libraries to mobile, rural, school, university and prison libraries, municipal and national libraries. Every library in Europe is eligible to take part in the Europe Challenge, from public libraries to mobile, rural, school, university, and prison libraries, municipal and national libraries.",,,2026-09-23 07:57:58.368390+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_641becbe2421,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/short-term-conference-and-travel-grant/,,Gulbenkian,en,Short Term Conference and Travel Scholarships,"Applicants must be: Studying or based in Armenia. Under 35 years old at the time of the application. A Master’s or PhD student, or a researcher from Armenia, wishing to attend international conferences, seminars, short-term courses or undertake research trips related to their field of study.",Short Term Conference and Travel Scholarships,"Applicants must be: Studying or based in Armenia. Under 35 years old at the time of the application. A Master’s or PhD student, or a researcher from Armenia, wishing to attend international conferences, seminars, short-term courses or undertake research trips related to their field of study.",End date 04 Dec 2026 / 23:59 Lisbon time,2026-12-04,2026-09-23 07:57:58.372875+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_951799db2821,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/short-term-grant-for-armenian-studies/,,Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation,en,Short Term Grant for Armenian Studies,"Eligibility Close Open Be (i) a Master or PhD degree student or (ii) a researcher in the field of Armenian Studies, wishing to conduct field research or pursue small research projects, or to engage in other relevant activities related to their work (including international conference attendance or summer school participation). The maximum duration of stay or length of project is three months. There is no age limit but preference is given to younger scholars. If you do not meet these requirements, then you are unlikely to be successful in your application. Note that if you are a researcher in Armenian Studies in Armenia wishing to participate in a conference or workshop abroad, you should apply to the Short Term Conference and Travel Grant for students and young academics in Armenia.",Short Term Grant for Armenian Studies,"Eligibility Close Open Be (i) a Master or PhD degree student or (ii) a researcher in the field of Armenian Studies, wishing to conduct field research or pursue small research projects, or to engage in other relevant activities related to their work (including international conference attendance or summer school participation). The maximum duration of stay or length of project is three months. There is no age limit but preference is given to younger scholars. If you do not meet these requirements, then you are unlikely to be successful in your application. Note that if you are a researcher in Armenian Studies in Armenia wishing to participate in a conference or workshop abroad, you should apply to the Short Term Conference and Travel Grant for students and young academics in Armenia.",Date Start date 19 Jan 2026 / 00:00 End date 04 Dec 2026 / 23:59 Lisbon time,2026-12-04,2026-09-23 07:57:58.387129+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_18eda3300a18,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/fellowships-gulbenkian-institute-for-advanced-study/,,Gulbenkian Institute for Advanced Study,en,Fellowships Gulbenkian Institute for Advanced Study,"The GIAS will host international academics, but will also consider applications from emeriti, independent scholars, and artists. Applications in most non-laboratorial and non-experimental fields will be considered, provided that the proposed work is not primarily practice- or application-oriented.",Fellowships Gulbenkian Institute for Advanced Study,"The GIAS will host international academics, but will also consider applications from emeriti, independent scholars, and artists. Applications in most non-laboratorial and non-experimental fields will be considered, provided that the proposed work is not primarily practice- or application-oriented.",End date 15 Oct 2026 / 15:00 Lisbon time,2026-10-15,2026-09-23 07:57:58.391323+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_9db5c1bb86df,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/visiting-professorships-in-the-humanities/,,Gulbenkian,en,Visiting Professorships in the Humanities,"Only Portuguese Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) are eligible, and the proposed academic activities must take place in Portugal. Applications must be submitted by the professor responsible for coordinating the visit, on behalf of the Portuguese HEI. The visiting professor is not eligible to apply directly.",Visiting Professorships in the Humanities,"Only Portuguese Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) are eligible, and the proposed academic activities must take place in Portugal. Applications must be submitted by the professor responsible for coordinating the visit, on behalf of the Portuguese HEI. The visiting professor is not eligible to apply directly.",30 Sep 2026 / 17:00 Lisbon time,2026-09-30,2026-09-23 07:57:58.397037+00:00
