Applications may be submitted by higher education lecturers, nationals and residents of a PALOP – Portuguese Language Speaking African Country (Angola, Cape Verde, Guinea Bissau, Mozambique, Sao Tome and Principe), who wish to undertake an advanced scientific internship at university institutions and research centres in Portugal with the purpose of beginning or consolidating their research activities in the fields of either Mathematics or Physics. Applicants should, at the least, hold a Master's Degree. Applicants holding Doctoral Degrees are also eligible for this tender. The maximum number of internships receiving support, for both Master's Degree and Doctoral Degree holders, is 15 with 10 in the field of Mathematics and similar and 5 in the field of Physics and similar.

May I apply while residing in Portugal in 2026?
No. Only applications from candidates residing in their countries of origin are eligible.

I work in a private Higher Education Institution. Am I eligible for this tender?
Yes. Members of staff working in the private sector may apply despite applications from lecturers and researchers working in the public sector being valued higher.

I have already been a Foundation grant holder. Am I eligible for this tender?
Yes. Past grant holders in this or another tender may also apply. However, you are not eligible when having already received a study grant supported by the Gulbenkian Foundation for 2026.

I am a student. Am I eligible for this tender?
Only when a student on a post-graduate program in the fields of Mathematics or Physics (Doctoral Degree) in employment at a higher education institution. In this case, and when holding a Master's Degree, you are eligible to apply to the candidate group with the Master's Degree level.",08 Jun 2026 / 16:00 Lisbon time,2026-06-08,2026-09-23 07:57:58.412261+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_87ad3b871ddc,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/envolve-phd/,,Gulbenkian,en,Envolve-PhD Health Sciences Research grants for doctoral students from PALOP countries,"Have a doctoral thesis project approved by the scientific council of a higher education institution; Hold an undergraduate degree from a higher education institution in a PALOP country (Angola, Cabo Verde, Guinea-Bissau, Mozambique or São Tomé and Príncipe); Be under 38 years of age on 31 December 2026.",Envolve-PhD Health Sciences Research grants for doctoral students from PALOP countries,"Have a doctoral thesis project approved by the scientific council of a higher education institution; Hold an undergraduate degree from a higher education institution in a PALOP country (Angola, Cabo Verde, Guinea-Bissau, Mozambique or São Tomé and Príncipe); Be under 38 years of age on 31 December 2026.",15 Jun 2026 / 17:00 Lisbon time,2026-06-15,2026-09-23 07:57:58.416859+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_fb365051dabf,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/masters-scholarships-for-students-from-palop/,,Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation,en,Master’s Scholarships for Students from PALOP,"Applicants must have permanent residence in their country of origin. Applicants must be applying for a master’s degree (applications for integrated master’s programs will not be considered) in the fields of mathematics, physics, chemistry and biology Applicants must hold a bachelor’s degree from a university in their country of origin, with a minimum grade average of 14 (on a scale of 0 to 20). The maximum age for application is 30 years (applicants must have been born in or after 1996).",Master’s Scholarships for Students from PALOP,"Applicants must have permanent residence in their country of origin. Applicants must be applying for a master’s degree (applications for integrated master’s programs will not be considered) in the fields of mathematics, physics, chemistry and biology Applicants must hold a bachelor’s degree from a university in their country of origin, with a minimum grade average of 14 (on a scale of 0 to 20). The maximum age for application is 30 years (applicants must have been born in or after 1996).",End date 08 Jun 2026 / 15:00 Lisbon time,2026-06-08,2026-09-23 07:57:58.420774+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_72289dc91d51,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/scholarships-for-arts-training-abroad/,,Gulbenkian Foundation,en,Scholarships for Arts Training Abroad,"Applications are open to Portuguese and foreign nationals who are resident in Portugal. For academic training, scholarships are awarded for postgraduate courses and master’s degrees. Applicants must be aged 35 or under on 31 December 2026. Priority will be given to early-career applicants who begin their course from 1 September 2026 onwards. For technical training and artistic development, scholarships support training projects aimed at specialisation, ongoing professional development and career advancement. There is no age limit for this category. Priority will be given to applicants whose training begins from 1 September 2026 onwards. In the field of music, applications are only accepted for specialisations in orchestral instruments, voice and conducting. Applications for undergraduate or doctoral degrees are not eligible. Applications in the fields of Architecture and Urbanism, Design, Art History, Heritage and Archaeology are not accepted.",Scholarships for Arts Training Abroad,"Applications are open to Portuguese and foreign nationals who are resident in Portugal. For academic training, scholarships are awarded for postgraduate courses and master’s degrees. Applicants must be aged 35 or under on 31 December 2026. Priority will be given to early-career applicants who begin their course from 1 September 2026 onwards. For technical training and artistic development, scholarships support training projects aimed at specialisation, ongoing professional development and career advancement. There is no age limit for this category. Priority will be given to applicants whose training begins from 1 September 2026 onwards. In the field of music, applications are only accepted for specialisations in orchestral instruments, voice and conducting. Applications for undergraduate or doctoral degrees are not eligible. Applications in the fields of Architecture and Urbanism, Design, Art History, Heritage and Archaeology are not accepted.",30 Apr 2026 / 15:00 Lisbon time,2026-04-30,2026-09-23 07:57:58.425445+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_9353c02dbbc6,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/higher-education-scholarships-for-armenian-students-in-from-developing-countries/,,Gulbenkian Foundation,en,Higher Education Scholarships for Armenian Students in Developing Countries,"Be of Armenian origin. Be resident in Lebanon or another developing country in the Middle East; Be no more than 25 years old at the time of the application. Demonstrate outstanding academic and/or examination results; Be enrolled or accepted in a higher education institution, duly recognized by the local national authorities. Be experiencing financial hardship; Declare to the Gulbenkian Foundation any other scholarships received for the purpose of obtaining their degree.",Higher Education Scholarships for Armenian Students in Developing Countries,"Be of Armenian origin. Be resident in Lebanon or another developing country in the Middle East; Be no more than 25 years old at the time of the application. Demonstrate outstanding academic and/or examination results; Be enrolled or accepted in a higher education institution, duly recognized by the local national authorities. Be experiencing financial hardship; Declare to the Gulbenkian Foundation any other scholarships received for the purpose of obtaining their degree.",30 Jun 2026 / 23:59,2026-06-30,2026-09-23 07:57:58.429202+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_d27e2a237d8e,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/calouste-gulbenkian-armenian-studies-scholarship/,,Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation,en,Calouste Gulbenkian Armenian Studies Scholarships,"Be admitted to, or already pursuing, a Master’s or PhD degree, or a Postdoctoral project focused on (contemporary) Armenian-related topics from a social sciences perspective, at an internationally recognised higher education institution, in the academic year for which the scholarship is sought. Have a designated academic supervisor or supervisory committee. Where a supervisor has not yet been formally appointed, applicants must provide a justification. For Postdoctoral applicants, a letter confirming institutional affiliation or equivalent documentation must be submitted in lieu of a supervisor or committee.",Calouste Gulbenkian Armenian Studies Scholarships,"Be admitted to, or already pursuing, a Master’s or PhD degree, or a Postdoctoral project focused on (contemporary) Armenian-related topics from a social sciences perspective, at an internationally recognised higher education institution, in the academic year for which the scholarship is sought. Have a designated academic supervisor or supervisory committee. Where a supervisor has not yet been formally appointed, applicants must provide a justification. For Postdoctoral applicants, a letter confirming institutional affiliation or equivalent documentation must be submitted in lieu of a supervisor or committee.",15 May 2026 / 23:59,2026-05-15,2026-09-23 07:57:58.433033+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_f055ef76a815,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/gulbenkian-explore-talent-school-olympiads/,,Gulbenkian,en,Gulbenkian Explore Talent Scholarships – School Olympiads,Students may apply if they: Have been winners or finalists in a School Olympiad held in Portugal during the 2025/2026 academic year; Are enrolled in the 10th or 11th year of secondary education in 2026/2027; Are available to participate in the meetings in Lisbon.,Gulbenkian Explore Talent Scholarships – School Olympiads,Students may apply if they: Have been winners or finalists in a School Olympiad held in Portugal during the 2025/2026 academic year; Are enrolled in the 10th or 11th year of secondary education in 2026/2027; Are available to participate in the meetings in Lisbon.,11 Jul 2026 / 17:00 Lisbon Time,2026-07-11,2026-09-23 07:57:58.438091+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_3e4681351a01,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/gulbenkian-research-scholarships-on-portuguese-culture/,,Gulbenkian,en,Gulbenkian Research Scholarships on Portuguese Culture for Foreigners,The call is aimed at non-Portuguese doctoral students and senior researchers who reside abroad and wish to conduct research in Portugal.,Gulbenkian Research Scholarships on Portuguese Culture for Foreigners,The call is aimed at non-Portuguese doctoral students and senior researchers who reside abroad and wish to conduct research in Portugal.,30 Jan 2026 / 15:00 Lisbon time,2026-01-30,2026-09-23 07:57:58.451357+00:00
italian_council_11306f3473a0,italian_council,https://creativitacontemporanea.cultura.gov.it/italiancouncil-edizione15/,https://portalebandidgcc.cultura.gov.it/,Direzione Generale Creatività Contemporanea del Ministero della Cultura,it,Italian Council – Edizione 15,"Possono presentare domanda di partecipazione: Ambiti 1 e 2 > Enti pubblici e privati senza scopo di lucro, sia italiani che stranieri (come musei, istituti universitari, fondazioni, associazioni culturali, comitati formalmente costituiti). È possibile richiedere un contributo non superiore all’80% del costo totale del progetto , con un tetto massimo che varia in base alla tipologia del progetto. I progetti devono svolgersi tra il 1° luglio 2026 e il 31 agosto 2028 . Ambito 3 > Artisti, fotografi, critici, curatori e altri professionisti dell’arte e della fotografia contemporanee, con cittadinanza italiana o fiscalmente residenti in Italia, che rispondano ai requisiti dell’avviso pubblico.",Italian Council – 15th Edition,"Eligible applicants: Areas 1 and 2 > Public and private non-profit entities, both Italian and foreign (such as museums, university institutes, foundations, cultural associations, formally constituted committees). It is possible to request a contribution not exceeding 80% of the total project cost, with a maximum cap that varies according to the type of project. Projects must take place between 1 July 2026 and 31 August 2028. Area 3 > Artists, photographers, critics, curators, and other contemporary art and photography professionals, with Italian citizenship or tax residence in Italy, who meet the requirements of the public notice.",31 marzo 2026 alle ore 15.00 (ora italiana),2026-09-23,2026-09-23 07:57:59.832483+00:00
