kunst_dk_denmark_28c59766a0db,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/exhibition-of-danish-art-abroad,https://portal.slks.dk//TAS_Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=7062179a8b2e49e1835fe8c4cd354c60,Danish Arts Foundation,en,Exhibition of Danish Art Abroad,Who may apply? You can apply if you plan to produce an art piece to be exhibited in Denmark or abroad And You can apply if you shall exhibit and/or promote the work of living visual artists in Denmark or abroad.,Exhibition of Danish Art Abroad,Who may apply? You can apply if you plan to produce an art piece to be exhibited in Denmark or abroad And You can apply if you shall exhibit and/or promote the work of living visual artists in Denmark or abroad.,"24.09.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 07:58:03.715604+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_83c3b68dac03,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/visual-arts-international-research-programme,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=14cde2fa1f14488ea90a43972c3a47d5,Danish Arts Foundation / Danish Art Foundation's Committee for Visual Arts Project Funding,en,Curatorial Research Programme,"Who may apply? Curators, directors of exhibition venues, art critics and art mediators working with contemporary art. Danish art institutions or other Danish art professionals can apply on behalf of one or more foreign curators, provided that the Danish actor undertakes programming and hosting the foreign curator's visit to Denmark. Applicants with Danish CVR/CPR/ NemKonto must apply via the Danish version of this pool The programme is primarily aimed at applicants who already have contacts on the Danish art scene or candidates who wish to develop a project involving specific Danish artists or institutions. Applicants must be able to organize meetings and studio visits on their own.",Curatorial Research Programme,"Who may apply? Curators, directors of exhibition venues, art critics and art mediators working with contemporary art. Danish art institutions or other Danish art professionals can apply on behalf of one or more foreign curators, provided that the Danish actor undertakes programming and hosting the foreign curator's visit to Denmark. Applicants with Danish CVR/CPR/ NemKonto must apply via the Danish version of this pool The programme is primarily aimed at applicants who already have contacts on the Danish art scene or candidates who wish to develop a project involving specific Danish artists or institutions. Applicants must be able to organize meetings and studio visits on their own.","24.09.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 07:58:03.719781+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_823c0bbbc582,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/performing-arts-international-activities,https://portal.slks.dk//TAS_Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=2f02cef278c24c4b80a20035ff8119a1,Danish Arts Foundation,en,Performing arts: International activities,"Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.

Who may apply? Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities.

Who may not apply? Support cannot be granted for projects, which are carried out exclusively by the large institutional theatres. By large institutional theatres we mean The Royal Danish Theatre, the Danish regional theatres, the Jutland Opera, and the theatres in the Copenhagen theatre association may not apply.

You cannot receive funding for the following purposes activities initiated ahead of the deadline educational purposes for individuals",Performing arts: International activities,"Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.

Who may apply? Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities.

Who may not apply? Support cannot be granted for projects, which are carried out exclusively by the large institutional theatres. By large institutional theatres we mean The Royal Danish Theatre, the Danish regional theatres, the Jutland Opera, and the theatres in the Copenhagen theatre association may not apply.

You cannot receive funding for the following purposes activities initiated ahead of the deadline educational purposes for individuals","01.10.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-01-10,2026-09-23 07:58:03.723024+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_091f95df035c,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/nordic-translations,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=e6330c53cf004a46b91c8f2972825f37,Danish Arts Foundation,en,Nordic translations,"Nordic publishers wishing to publish a work translated from Danish into another Nordic language. Non-Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Literary production and translation’. Applications should be made in the Nordic country in which the work was originally published. For the translation of works from Danish, you should therefore submit your application to the Danish Arts Foundation's Committee for Literary Project Funding. Before submitting the application, the applicant must have acquired the copyrights for the literary work and signed a contract with a translator. Projects may not be finished before the expiry of the application deadline.",Nordic translations,"Nordic publishers wishing to publish a work translated from Danish into another Nordic language. Non-Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Literary production and translation’. Applications should be made in the Nordic country in which the work was originally published. For the translation of works from Danish, you should therefore submit your application to the Danish Arts Foundation's Committee for Literary Project Funding. Before submitting the application, the applicant must have acquired the copyrights for the literary work and signed a contract with a translator. Projects may not be finished before the expiry of the application deadline.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 07:58:03.727060+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_be0b1bc26009,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/literary-production-and-translation,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=6710d33dda9c469aa7c4ad376579223f,Danish Arts Foundation,en,Literary production and translation,"Who may apply? Publishing houses and other publishers of Danish literary works in translation, (organisations etc.) Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Nordiske oversættelser/Nordic translations’ YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Publication of literature in various formats translated from Danish. If you are applying for grants to cover both production and translation costs, you must apply in a single, combined application per work. You can only apply when you have acquired the rights to the work and signed a contract with the translator named in the application. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Individuals cannot apply for support for translation. The support must be applied for by the publishing publisher. Translation of Danish titles to other Nordic languages. Nordic publishers may apply to the Fund for Nordic Translations/ puljen Nordiske Oversættelser for funding to cover fees for translators who translate a work from Danish into another Nordic language Publication of works in which the literature belongs to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature.",Literary production and translation,"Who may apply? Publishing houses and other publishers of Danish literary works in translation, (organisations etc.) Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Nordiske oversættelser/Nordic translations’ YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Publication of literature in various formats translated from Danish. If you are applying for grants to cover both production and translation costs, you must apply in a single, combined application per work. You can only apply when you have acquired the rights to the work and signed a contract with the translator named in the application. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Individuals cannot apply for support for translation. The support must be applied for by the publishing publisher. Translation of Danish titles to other Nordic languages. Nordic publishers may apply to the Fund for Nordic Translations/ puljen Nordiske Oversættelser for funding to cover fees for translators who translate a work from Danish into another Nordic language Publication of works in which the literature belongs to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 07:58:03.730557+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_92d5217dc912,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/sample-translations-from-danish,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=bf0a14e4c53a42ae856ca862b96a669e,Danish Arts Foundation / Statens Kunstfond,en,Sample translations from Danish,"Who may apply? Danish and foreign publishers and agencies. Note: In order to ensure the spreading of art support, you may apply for support for a total of four sample translations.

YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR:
Sample translation of a Danish work into a foreign language.

YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR:
Sample translations of works that the committee assesses belong to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature.
Sample translations of your own works or text revisions.
Projects that were carried out and finished before the expiry of the application deadline.",Sample translations from Danish,"Who may apply? Danish and foreign publishers and agencies. Note: In order to ensure the spreading of art support, you may apply for support for a total of four sample translations.

