kunsten_be_flanders_04af2c6c6f4a,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/want-to-show-your-artwork-in-a-museum-join-nationale-expo-nationale/,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/want-to-show-your-artwork-in-a-museum-join-nationale-expo-nationale/,museumPASSmusées,en,Want to show your artwork in a museum? Join Nationale Expo Nationale!,"Anyone engaged in visual arts can submit an artwork. Everyone aged 18 years or more is welcome to participate. The only request is that your work must be inspired by the theme “natural”. It should explore nature that is not static, but rather grows, migrates, and constantly adapts.",Want to show your artwork in a museum? Join Nationale Expo Nationale!,"Anyone engaged in visual arts can submit an artwork. Everyone aged 18 years or more is welcome to participate. The only request is that your work must be inspired by the theme “natural”. It should explore nature that is not static, but rather grows, migrates, and constantly adapts.",02 Dec 2026,2026-12-02,2026-09-23 07:58:03.751423+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_0c520b567ceb,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-2027-curatorial-research-fellowship/,https://rencontresarles.typeform.com/to/WnwfW8TP,Arles - Les Rencontres de la photographie,en,Call for 2027 curatorial research fellowship,"The Rencontres d’Arles curatorial research grant is aimed at exhibition curators wishing to carry out an original project relating to image or photography.

The application form must contain the following documents, in the order listed below, in a single PDF file (maximum 10 MB):
→ a description of the proposed exhibition project for the research grant (maximum 5,000 characters), a list of the works and artists considered for the project (it is strongly recommended that visuals be provided), a provisional research budget (5,000 euros), a research timetable and a provisional budget for the production of the exhibition (15,000 euros) within the allocated budgets.
→ a biography of the curator (or co-curators/collective, where applicable), including educational background, full contact details and a list of the curator(s)’ projects and exhibitions, featuring descriptions and images (in the case of exhibitions) of the various projects carried out by the curator(s).

Texts must be in French or English, ideally both.",Call for 2027 curatorial research fellowship,"The Rencontres d’Arles curatorial research grant is aimed at exhibition curators wishing to carry out an original project relating to image or photography.

The application form must contain the following documents, in the order listed below, in a single PDF file (maximum 10 MB):
→ a description of the proposed exhibition project for the research grant (maximum 5,000 characters), a list of the works and artists considered for the project (it is strongly recommended that visuals be provided), a provisional research budget (5,000 euros), a research timetable and a provisional budget for the production of the exhibition (15,000 euros) within the allocated budgets.
→ a biography of the curator (or co-curators/collective, where applicable), including educational background, full contact details and a list of the curator(s)’ projects and exhibitions, featuring descriptions and images (in the case of exhibitions) of the various projects carried out by the curator(s).

Texts must be in French or English, ideally both.",30 Nov 2026,2026-11-30,2026-09-23 07:58:03.754804+00:00
