kunsten_be_flanders_1c78c30f66d3,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-support-by-the-netherlands-embassy-in-belgium/,https://dutchculture.nl/en/news/open-call-support-dutch-embassy-brussels,Netherlands Embassy in Belgium,en,Open call for support by the Netherlands Embassy in Belgium,"Eligible for support are Dutch-Belgian co-projects across all disciplines, but special attention is given to the performing arts, contemporary visual arts, the creative industries (especially architecture, design, fashion and digital art), and cultural heritage. Multidisciplinary projects are also welcome. In addition, the embassy welcomes projects that explore innovative formats and presentation methods, cross-border cultural exchange, and initiatives that promote participation and inclusion, equal rights, and sustainability. Projects must take place in Belgium, unless they involve virtual collaboration. Special attention is given to projects taking place in Wallonia and the Meuse-Rhine Euregion. Note: only the Belgian partner can apply for this funding.",Open call for support by the Netherlands Embassy in Belgium,"Eligible for support are Dutch-Belgian co-projects across all disciplines, but special attention is given to the performing arts, contemporary visual arts, the creative industries (especially architecture, design, fashion and digital art), and cultural heritage. Multidisciplinary projects are also welcome. In addition, the embassy welcomes projects that explore innovative formats and presentation methods, cross-border cultural exchange, and initiatives that promote participation and inclusion, equal rights, and sustainability. Projects must take place in Belgium, unless they involve virtual collaboration. Special attention is given to projects taking place in Wallonia and the Meuse-Rhine Euregion. Note: only the Belgian partner can apply for this funding.",03 Nov 2026,2026-11-03,2026-09-23 07:58:03.765077+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_1e4f87dbc5b9,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/visualise-support-for-international-exhibition-projects-with-ukrainian-partners/,https://ui.org.ua/en/news-en/visualise-2026-international-exhibition-support-programme/,Ukrainian Institute,en,Visualise – support for international exhibition projects with Ukrainian partners,"The following entities are eligible to apply: legal bodies of all forms of ownership and private entrepreneurs registered in Ukraine with a confirmed prior experience of carrying out projects similar to the submitted one; organisations and companies registered outside of Ukraine, their branch offices and delegations registered and certified in Ukraine with a confirmed institutional capacity and prior experience of carrying out projects similar to the submitted one. Applications submitted by individuals, legal entities registered both in Ukraine and abroad, related to the aggressor state – the Russian Federation, which is recognized as such in accordance with the Law of Ukraine“ “On the Prohibition of Propaganda of the Russian Nazi Totalitarian Regime, Armed Aggression of the Russian Federation as a Terrorist State against Ukraine, Symbolism of the Military Invasion of the Russian Nazi Totalitarian Regime into Ukraine”№ 2265-ІХ of May 22, 2022, the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran, are considered ineligible, namely: legal entities with beneficiaries who are individuals – citizens of the aggressor state of the Russian Federation, the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran or or legal entities associated with the aggressor state of the Russian Federation and the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran; legal entities or individual enterpreneurs and / or participants of such entities to whom personal special economic and other restrictive measures (sanctions) have been applied in accordance with the Law of Ukraine “On Sanctions” and decisions of the National Security and Defense Council of Ukraine; You can familiarize yourself with the current sanctions list on the website of the Verkhovna Rada of Ukraine at the link: https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/n0004525-20#Text legal entities or individual enterpreneurs and / or participants of such entities or individuals who have violated the Law of Ukraine “On Ensuring the Rights and Freedoms of Citizens and the Legal Regime in the Temporarily Occupied Territory of Ukraine” dated 15.04.2014 №  1207-VII. Technical requirements The submitted applications must comply with the following technical requirements : The project is being implemented in cooperation between Ukrainian and international institution(s) or organisation(s) (museum, gallery, fair, festival, etc. in the country of the project implementation) that have the institutional capacity and experience in implementing similar projects and / or objects of intellectual property that can be used in the process of carrying out the exhibition project and organising the exhibition.  List of recommended partnership institutions abroad available here . The project is being implemented in one of the Ukrainian Institute’s target countries as of 2026 (The Republic of Poland, the Federal Republic of Germany, the French Republic, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland, the Slovak Republic, the United States of America, the Kingdom of the Netherlands, the Republic of Lithuania,  the Republic of South Africa, the Federative Republic of Brazil, the United Mexican States, the Argentine Republic, the Republic of India, the Republic of Indonesia,Hungary). The Ukrainian Institute reserves the right to implement exhibition projects in other countries on a case-by-case basis. The project showcases Ukrainian photography and/or addresses the overarching themes of the Ukrainian Institute’s activities: Russia’s War Against Ukraine Ukraine’s Recovery and Future Civil Society as the Foundation of Statehood Crimea and the Crimean Tatars Decolonization of culture and reappropriation of cultural heritage Iconic figures, phenomena, and events The Ukrainian Institute reserves the right to support the implementation of selected projects on other topics, depending on the circumstances The start of the project is scheduled no earlier than March 1, 2027. The application is submitted in due time. The application is submitted in accordance with the provided form in Ukrainian (and if necessary in English). All necessary supporting documentation in accordance with the requirements below has been summitted. Each section of the application is filled in without exceeding the number of characters specified in the application form.",Visualise – support for international exhibition projects with Ukrainian partners,"The following entities are eligible to apply: legal bodies of all forms of ownership and private entrepreneurs registered in Ukraine with a confirmed prior experience of carrying out projects similar to the submitted one; organisations and companies registered outside of Ukraine, their branch offices and delegations registered and certified in Ukraine with a confirmed institutional capacity and prior experience of carrying out projects similar to the submitted one. Applications submitted by individuals, legal entities registered both in Ukraine and abroad, related to the aggressor state – the Russian Federation, which is recognized as such in accordance with the Law of Ukraine“ “On the Prohibition of Propaganda of the Russian Nazi Totalitarian Regime, Armed Aggression of the Russian Federation as a Terrorist State against Ukraine, Symbolism of the Military Invasion of the Russian Nazi Totalitarian Regime into Ukraine”№ 2265-ІХ of May 22, 2022, the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran, are considered ineligible, namely: legal entities with beneficiaries who are individuals – citizens of the aggressor state of the Russian Federation, the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran or or legal entities associated with the aggressor state of the Russian Federation and the Republic of Belarus and/or the Islamic Republic of Iran; legal entities or individual enterpreneurs and / or participants of such entities to whom personal special economic and other restrictive measures (sanctions) have been applied in accordance with the Law of Ukraine “On Sanctions” and decisions of the National Security and Defense Council of Ukraine; You can familiarize yourself with the current sanctions list on the website of the Verkhovna Rada of Ukraine at the link: https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/n0004525-20#Text legal entities or individual enterpreneurs and / or participants of such entities or individuals who have violated the Law of Ukraine “On Ensuring the Rights and Freedoms of Citizens and the Legal Regime in the Temporarily Occupied Territory of Ukraine” dated 15.04.2014 №  1207-VII. Technical requirements The submitted applications must comply with the following technical requirements : The project is being implemented in cooperation between Ukrainian and international institution(s) or organisation(s) (museum, gallery, fair, festival, etc. in the country of the project implementation) that have the institutional capacity and experience in implementing similar projects and / or objects of intellectual property that can be used in the process of carrying out the exhibition project and organising the exhibition.  List of recommended partnership institutions abroad available here . The project is being implemented in one of the Ukrainian Institute’s target countries as of 2026 (The Republic of Poland, the Federal Republic of Germany, the French Republic, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland, the Slovak Republic, the United States of America, the Kingdom of the Netherlands, the Republic of Lithuania,  the Republic of South Africa, the Federative Republic of Brazil, the United Mexican States, the Argentine Republic, the Republic of India, the Republic of Indonesia,Hungary). The Ukrainian Institute reserves the right to implement exhibition projects in other countries on a case-by-case basis. The project showcases Ukrainian photography and/or addresses the overarching themes of the Ukrainian Institute’s activities: Russia’s War Against Ukraine Ukraine’s Recovery and Future Civil Society as the Foundation of Statehood Crimea and the Crimean Tatars Decolonization of culture and reappropriation of cultural heritage Iconic figures, phenomena, and events The Ukrainian Institute reserves the right to support the implementation of selected projects on other topics, depending on the circumstances The start of the project is scheduled no earlier than March 1, 2027. The application is submitted in due time. The application is submitted in accordance with the provided form in Ukrainian (and if necessary in English). All necessary supporting documentation in accordance with the requirements below has been summitted. Each section of the application is filled in without exceeding the number of characters specified in the application form.",01 Nov 2026,2026-11-01,2026-09-23 07:58:03.768492+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_d62c210c4b06,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/premiere-concours/,https://festivita.be/premierecompetition/,Festi Vita!,en,“PREMIÈRE” CONCOURS,"Dedicated to music performed on period instruments, cs by highlighting the uniqueness of their artistic, scholarly, and interpretive approaches. It is precisely this subtle balance of qualities that the event strives to reveal to an open and enthusiastic audience.

The aim here is to highlight small ensembles of the new generation, capable of bringing the competition’s three objectives—artistic, scientific, and rhetorical—into dialogue with brilliance and originality.

The selection of candidates is based on a subtle balance between three complementary approaches. First, it evaluates the artistic dimension through the quality of musical performance. It then relies on a rigorous scientific approach, which examines the relevance of research and the highlighting of historical practices (style, ornamentation, improvisation, instrumentation, pronunciation, basso continuo, temperament, placement of musicians, etc.). Finally, the rhetorical dimension crowns this process by rewarding the quality of communication with the audience: through an original and creative oral presentation—delivered in French, Dutch, or English—the musicians are invited to foster greater receptivity and build a genuine connection with their audience.",“PREMIÈRE” CONCOURS,"Dedicated to music performed on period instruments, cs by highlighting the uniqueness of their artistic, scholarly, and interpretive approaches. It is precisely this subtle balance of qualities that the event strives to reveal to an open and enthusiastic audience.

The aim here is to highlight small ensembles of the new generation, capable of bringing the competition’s three objectives—artistic, scientific, and rhetorical—into dialogue with brilliance and originality.

The selection of candidates is based on a subtle balance between three complementary approaches. First, it evaluates the artistic dimension through the quality of musical performance. It then relies on a rigorous scientific approach, which examines the relevance of research and the highlighting of historical practices (style, ornamentation, improvisation, instrumentation, pronunciation, basso continuo, temperament, placement of musicians, etc.). Finally, the rhetorical dimension crowns this process by rewarding the quality of communication with the audience: through an original and creative oral presentation—delivered in French, Dutch, or English—the musicians are invited to foster greater receptivity and build a genuine connection with their audience.",01 Nov 2026,2026-11-01,2026-09-23 07:58:03.771665+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2c25abbd7783,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/premiere-concours-2027/,https://festivita.be/premierecompetition/,FestiVita! Brussels Early Music Festival,en,Première Concours 2027,"The Première Early Music competition on historical instruments seeks to promote young musicians who bring their artistic, scholarly, and rhetorical approach to the fore.",Première Concours 2027,"The Première Early Music competition on historical instruments seeks to promote young musicians who bring their artistic, scholarly, and rhetorical approach to the fore.",01 Nov 2026,2026-11-01,2026-09-23 07:58:03.775033+00:00
