kunsten_be_flanders_9c1b52c8ff2d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-teatri-riflessi-festival-2027-international-short-performance-competition/,https://www.iterculture.eu/en/teatri-riflessi/tr2027/tr12/,Teatri Riflessi Festival,en,Open Call Teatri Riflessi Festival 2027 – International Short Performance Competition,"Teatri Riflessi Festival has opened its 2027 call for short performances: live works no longer than 15 minutes of contemporary dance, theatre, circus or multidisciplinary performance.",Open Call Teatri Riflessi Festival 2027 – International Short Performance Competition,"Teatri Riflessi Festival has opened its 2027 call for short performances: live works no longer than 15 minutes of contemporary dance, theatre, circus or multidisciplinary performance.",15 October 2026 (17:00 CEST),2026-10-15,2026-09-23 07:58:03.785300+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_81744cb359a1,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/support-for-international-showcasing-of-co-creation-projects/,https://zmina.eu/en/calls/zmina-resilience-showcasing,IZOLYATSIA Foundation (UA) and Malý Berlín (SK) together with Trans Europe Halles (SE),en,Support for International Showcasing of co-creation projects,"rolling open call for cultural and arts organisations within the ZMINA:Resilience project, strand “Support for international showcasing of co-creation projects” . The objective of this call is to support projects that bring artistic and cultural works co-created by Ukrainian and other Creative Europe cultural organisations to wider audiences through public showcasing and presentation events in Ukraine and across other Creative Europe countries. Funding will be provided to projects featuring co-creations made by partnerships involving at least one organisation from Ukraine and at least one organisation from another Creative Europe country. The projects should maximise the visibility, audience reach, sustainability, and future showcasing potential of these works. Supported projects are expected to include active partner cooperation to adapt showcased works to new audiences, for example by contextualising works, providing translation, involving local artists, experts and communities, conducting parallel programmes, and similar approaches. All creative and cultural sectors are eligible except audiovisual. Project Objectives Showcase and tour co-creations that explore the theme of resilience in any arts or cultural sector except audiovisual. Hold a minimum of 6 public presentation events: at least 3 events in each of at least two countries, one of which must be Ukraine. The presentation events cannot take place in the home city or town of any of the applicant organisations.",Support for International Showcasing of co-creation projects,"rolling open call for cultural and arts organisations within the ZMINA:Resilience project, strand “Support for international showcasing of co-creation projects” . The objective of this call is to support projects that bring artistic and cultural works co-created by Ukrainian and other Creative Europe cultural organisations to wider audiences through public showcasing and presentation events in Ukraine and across other Creative Europe countries. Funding will be provided to projects featuring co-creations made by partnerships involving at least one organisation from Ukraine and at least one organisation from another Creative Europe country. The projects should maximise the visibility, audience reach, sustainability, and future showcasing potential of these works. Supported projects are expected to include active partner cooperation to adapt showcased works to new audiences, for example by contextualising works, providing translation, involving local artists, experts and communities, conducting parallel programmes, and similar approaches. All creative and cultural sectors are eligible except audiovisual. Project Objectives Showcase and tour co-creations that explore the theme of resilience in any arts or cultural sector except audiovisual. Hold a minimum of 6 public presentation events: at least 3 events in each of at least two countries, one of which must be Ukraine. The presentation events cannot take place in the home city or town of any of the applicant organisations.",14 Oct 2026,2026-10-14,2026-09-23 07:58:03.788531+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_5de8a9a589b6,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-film-projects-sic-2027/,https://soundimageculture.org/call-for-projects/,SoundImageCulture,en,Call for Film Projects: SIC 2027,"What we look for We are looking for projects that are singular, authentic and push the borders of audiovisual language. Our aim is to support the participant to develop their artistic vision fully. We give priority to projects that already have visual materials, footage, sounds, photos.

What We Expect To be present at the collective sessions To bring new materials (rushes, edits, try-outs) to every session To hold at least one meeting (max. 2 hours) with your personal coach in between sessions To give feedback and assistance to your peers

Selection Our selection is based on a project proposal for a film. In one document, answer the following questions (maximum 2 x A4 pages): What is the subject of your project and why do you want to make it? What is the relation between you and your subject? What is the formal approach that you envision for the film? Is there a relation between your subject and the form you choose? Save this document as a PDF and upload it using the application form (on the website). Feel free to add images to the document, as additional pages (max. 5 MB in total). Documents with text exceeding 2 pages will be rejected. In the form below: In one link, of a maximum duration of 8 minutes, share your previous work(s) and/or audiovisual materials related to the project. This is not mandatory, but is very important to us. Please verify link and password (if any) before sending them. Please subtitle your video in English (we will not watch your video without subtitles).

Application Procedure To send us your application, complete the following steps by Monday 12 October 2026 at 12pm noon (Brussels time) by completing the form below Upload the PDF document describing your project and answering the three questions (see above) Upload your CV (maximum 2 pages) Upload your profile picture + three visuals that accompany your film proposal. The profile picture and the visuals will be published on our website if your project is selected. Please note that the language of submission is English (please subtitle audiovisual material) and that incomplete applications will not be considered.",Call for Film Projects: SIC 2027,"What we look for We are looking for projects that are singular, authentic and push the borders of audiovisual language. Our aim is to support the participant to develop their artistic vision fully. We give priority to projects that already have visual materials, footage, sounds, photos.

What We Expect To be present at the collective sessions To bring new materials (rushes, edits, try-outs) to every session To hold at least one meeting (max. 2 hours) with your personal coach in between sessions To give feedback and assistance to your peers

Selection Our selection is based on a project proposal for a film. In one document, answer the following questions (maximum 2 x A4 pages): What is the subject of your project and why do you want to make it? What is the relation between you and your subject? What is the formal approach that you envision for the film? Is there a relation between your subject and the form you choose? Save this document as a PDF and upload it using the application form (on the website). Feel free to add images to the document, as additional pages (max. 5 MB in total). Documents with text exceeding 2 pages will be rejected. In the form below: In one link, of a maximum duration of 8 minutes, share your previous work(s) and/or audiovisual materials related to the project. This is not mandatory, but is very important to us. Please verify link and password (if any) before sending them. Please subtitle your video in English (we will not watch your video without subtitles).

Application Procedure To send us your application, complete the following steps by Monday 12 October 2026 at 12pm noon (Brussels time) by completing the form below Upload the PDF document describing your project and answering the three questions (see above) Upload your CV (maximum 2 pages) Upload your profile picture + three visuals that accompany your film proposal. The profile picture and the visuals will be published on our website if your project is selected. Please note that the language of submission is English (please subtitle audiovisual material) and that incomplete applications will not be considered.",12 Oct 2026,2026-10-12,2026-09-23 07:58:03.791611+00:00
