kunsten_be_flanders_6e69a631d20d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-concepts-steiger-gallery/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdTCGtV5h0Izt9VY1QmrLbIz2Ic3UMYAcip0LuuWJ01W5_qZw/viewform,Steiger Gallery,en,Call for Concepts – Steiger Gallery,"To apply, emerging and established artists from all disciplines are invited to participate. Regional, national, and international submissions are expressly encouraged.

Technique
No specific material or medium is prescribed for the realization of the artwork. In particular, the following media may be used: Light or media art, sculpture, sound Art, installative and interactive works, film, murals, kinetic artworks, land art, other techniques.

Prerequisite
The concepts must be feasible for the artists to implement independently. To protect the local wildlife, installations that produce loud bangs are excluded from the application process. Artworks containing racist, anti-Semitic, sexist, transphobic or ableist content, or which are otherwise inhumane or discriminatory, are excluded from participation. The concepts must be suitable for installation in a public outdoor space. In particular, weather conditions and the risk of vandalism must be taken into account when selecting materials and designing the construction.",Call for Concepts – Steiger Gallery,"To apply, emerging and established artists from all disciplines are invited to participate. Regional, national, and international submissions are expressly encouraged.

Technique
No specific material or medium is prescribed for the realization of the artwork. In particular, the following media may be used: Light or media art, sculpture, sound Art, installative and interactive works, film, murals, kinetic artworks, land art, other techniques.

Prerequisite
The concepts must be feasible for the artists to implement independently. To protect the local wildlife, installations that produce loud bangs are excluded from the application process. Artworks containing racist, anti-Semitic, sexist, transphobic or ableist content, or which are otherwise inhumane or discriminatory, are excluded from participation. The concepts must be suitable for installation in a public outdoor space. In particular, weather conditions and the risk of vandalism must be taken into account when selecting materials and designing the construction.",13 Sep 2026,2026-09-13,2026-09-23 07:58:03.821736+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_16f5933a3038,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-project-pitch-session-transnational-ensemble-collaborations/,,field notes / Time to Listen conference,en,Call: Project Pitch Session – Transnational Ensemble Collaborations,"We invite ensembles, collectives, artists and curators to present projects at the Time to Listen conference that explore creative forms of transnational collaboration in the independent music scene. We are looking for projects and approaches that go beyond conventional (international) co-production models and experiment with new ways of exchanging, producing together and sharing resources. These may include sustainable, solidarity-based or experimental forms of cooperation – between ensembles, within broader networks, or in constellations that deliberately question and rethink existing structures. Of particular interest are approaches that enable long-term collaboration, share knowledge and responsibility, and respond to current ecological, political and financial challenges. Projects at different stages of development are welcome, from initial ideas that are open to additional partners joining, to projects that have already been implemented – whether successfully or, equally welcome, unsuccessfully.",Call: Project Pitch Session – Transnational Ensemble Collaborations,"We invite ensembles, collectives, artists and curators to present projects at the Time to Listen conference that explore creative forms of transnational collaboration in the independent music scene. We are looking for projects and approaches that go beyond conventional (international) co-production models and experiment with new ways of exchanging, producing together and sharing resources. These may include sustainable, solidarity-based or experimental forms of cooperation – between ensembles, within broader networks, or in constellations that deliberately question and rethink existing structures. Of particular interest are approaches that enable long-term collaboration, share knowledge and responsibility, and respond to current ecological, political and financial challenges. Projects at different stages of development are welcome, from initial ideas that are open to additional partners joining, to projects that have already been implemented – whether successfully or, equally welcome, unsuccessfully.",04 Sep 2026,2026-09-04,2026-09-23 07:58:03.826733+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_064cec6b0d25,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/neo-future-thematic-2-week-paid-residency-program-in-finland-dec-2026/,https://www.arteles.org/,Arteles Creative Center,en,"Neo Future – Thematic 2-week (paid) residency program in Finland, Dec 2026","Neo Future: Shifting into new realities is a special short-term residency for people reaching beyond the familiar and investigating what may emerge next. Artificial intelligence, expanded consciousness, human transformation, singularity, future societies and realities not yet named form an open field for creative research. The transdisciplinary program brings imagination, inquiry and experimentation together across art, science, design, technology, philosophy and unconventional forms of knowledge. It is process-focused rather than outcome-driven, creating space to question present assumptions, follow emerging ideas and develop perspectives that may not yet fit established categories.","Neo Future – Thematic 2-week (paid) residency program in Finland, Dec 2026","Neo Future: Shifting into new realities is a special short-term residency for people reaching beyond the familiar and investigating what may emerge next. Artificial intelligence, expanded consciousness, human transformation, singularity, future societies and realities not yet named form an open field for creative research. The transdisciplinary program brings imagination, inquiry and experimentation together across art, science, design, technology, philosophy and unconventional forms of knowledge. It is process-focused rather than outcome-driven, creating space to question present assumptions, follow emerging ideas and develop perspectives that may not yet fit established categories.",3 September 2026,2026-09-03,2026-09-23 07:58:03.831189+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2a53d6b47ce2,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/pairing-is-caring-2026-2027-op-zoek-naar-mentors/,https://framaforms.org/paring-is-caring-2026-1778770204,"Flanders Arts Institute, The Gap, NICC",en,Wanted: Mentors who would like to support emerging artists,This call for applications is aimed exclusively at mentors.,Wanted: Mentors who would like to support emerging artists,This call for applications is aimed exclusively at mentors.,01 Sep 2026,2026-09-01,2026-09-23 07:58:03.835750+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_32cfae041bea,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/lichtkunstwerk-voor-het-stadhuis-van-leuven/,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/lichtkunstwerk-voor-het-stadhuis-van-leuven/,"City of Leuven, LOV2030, Shift",en,Light artwork for Leuven Town Hall,"Candidates submit an application file explaining their project (max. 15 pages, excluding appendix). The file answers the following questions:
Artistic vision for the artwork. What are the theme and atmosphere of the artwork? How does the work relate to the town hall and, by extension, the historic city centre? What is its relationship with the audience?
Artistic vision for the process. What role do you see for the young people of Shift? How will you ensure that the young people feel ownership and involvement? How do you want to work with them, and how does that translate into a concrete working format? How will you ensure that one young person can easily make a small contribution, while another makes a larger one?
Initial outline of the technical production. What is technically necessary for the development of the project? Outline its feasibility. (See appendix for more information about the location and specific technical conditions.)
Include as an appendix an example of a previously realised project, including its technical plan and budget.",Light artwork for Leuven Town Hall,"Candidates submit an application file explaining their project (max. 15 pages, excluding appendix). The file answers the following questions:
Artistic vision for the artwork. What are the theme and atmosphere of the artwork? How does the work relate to the town hall and, by extension, the historic city centre? What is its relationship with the audience?
Artistic vision for the process. What role do you see for the young people of Shift? How will you ensure that the young people feel ownership and involvement? How do you want to work with them, and how does that translate into a concrete working format? How will you ensure that one young person can easily make a small contribution, while another makes a larger one?
Initial outline of the technical production. What is technically necessary for the development of the project? Outline its feasibility. (See appendix for more information about the location and specific technical conditions.)
Include as an appendix an example of a previously realised project, including its technical plan and budget.",1 September 2026,2026-09-01,2026-09-23 07:58:03.840430+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_027f9c38db13,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/residency-open-call-2027/,https://arteventura.eu/artists-in-residence/open-call,Arteventura,en,Residency Open Call 2027,"The application is open for all professional artists. Artists can apply individual, as a duo or in group. If you are applying as a duo, both artists have to fill in the application and have to mention the name of their partner. Groups are welcome up to 10 people. • Arteventura offers silence, space and time to engage in research and development. • To get an idea of your personal work we ask to send in a portfolio and a brief description of your artistic practice or research. • Add a motivation letter explaining why you want to stay at arteventura, what you expect from the residency and what you would like to achieve. • Arteventura is a sustainable (of-the-grid) project. We ask the artists to consider this and share our vision. Tell us in a few words how you support this vision. • We encourage artists to share the research or its results at the end of the residency. • We are very pleased when an artist leaves a work, however this is not mandatory. These works will enter the arteventura collection and will be shared with a wider audience. • Arteventura doesn’t receive any financial support. Running a residency has overhead costs and daily running costs. The residency fee contributes to pay a part of these costs. • We encourage selected artists to apply for grants and will provide invitation letters and other relevant information needed.",Residency Open Call 2027,"The application is open for all professional artists. Artists can apply individual, as a duo or in group. If you are applying as a duo, both artists have to fill in the application and have to mention the name of their partner. Groups are welcome up to 10 people. • Arteventura offers silence, space and time to engage in research and development. • To get an idea of your personal work we ask to send in a portfolio and a brief description of your artistic practice or research. • Add a motivation letter explaining why you want to stay at arteventura, what you expect from the residency and what you would like to achieve. • Arteventura is a sustainable (of-the-grid) project. We ask the artists to consider this and share our vision. Tell us in a few words how you support this vision. • We encourage artists to share the research or its results at the end of the residency. • We are very pleased when an artist leaves a work, however this is not mandatory. These works will enter the arteventura collection and will be shared with a wider audience. • Arteventura doesn’t receive any financial support. Running a residency has overhead costs and daily running costs. The residency fee contributes to pay a part of these costs. • We encourage selected artists to apply for grants and will provide invitation letters and other relevant information needed.",30 Aug 2026,2026-08-30,2026-09-23 07:58:03.843466+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_05cd80dee77f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/auditie-voor-fysieke-performers/,https://forms.gle/5v6C5gwkixyJoCPCA,Fabuleus,en,Auditions for physical performers,"We are looking for three professional performers (x/f/m) with good ball control. We are open to different disciplines and backgrounds: jugglers, freestyle footballers, dancers, physical actors. It is essential that you are curious about what you can do with balls of different shapes and sizes, and that you are interested in creating a movement-based performance using objects. You must be available during the rehearsal weeks (mostly at OPEK, Leuven) from June 2027. The premiere will take place in January 2028 at STUK Leuven. We are looking for performers who live in Belgium or who have accommodation in Belgium for the entire duration of the creation and tour.",Auditions for physical performers,"We are looking for three professional performers (x/f/m) with good ball control. We are open to different disciplines and backgrounds: jugglers, freestyle footballers, dancers, physical actors. It is essential that you are curious about what you can do with balls of different shapes and sizes, and that you are interested in creating a movement-based performance using objects. You must be available during the rehearsal weeks (mostly at OPEK, Leuven) from June 2027. The premiere will take place in January 2028 at STUK Leuven. We are looking for performers who live in Belgium or who have accommodation in Belgium for the entire duration of the creation and tour.","23 August 2026, 23:59.",2026-08-23,2026-09-23 07:58:03.848831+00:00
