kunsten_be_flanders_91a6541c6612,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-discover/,https://geuzenhuis.be/open-call-discover-ontwerp-de-cover-van-de-geus/,Geuzenhuis,en,Open call (DIS)COVER,"We invite young artistic talent (aged 18–30) to translate our core value of FREE THINKING into a powerful, contemporary cover for De Geus Magazine. Illustration, photography, graphic art or painting: the medium doesn’t matter. As long as it challenges, raises questions and doesn’t leave you indifferent. With (DIS)COVER, they aim to give young creators space to express themselves critically and socially. They are looking for an independent image that conveys humanistic values; it may be activist or playful and should encourage reflection (we’ll steer clear of explicit party politics). Humour or a more sober tone? Confrontational or unifying? The choice is yours. Formal training isn’t a must, but a desire to make your voice heard certainly is!",Open call (DIS)COVER,"We invite young artistic talent (aged 18–30) to translate our core value of FREE THINKING into a powerful, contemporary cover for De Geus Magazine. Illustration, photography, graphic art or painting: the medium doesn’t matter. As long as it challenges, raises questions and doesn’t leave you indifferent. With (DIS)COVER, they aim to give young creators space to express themselves critically and socially. They are looking for an independent image that conveys humanistic values; it may be activist or playful and should encourage reflection (we’ll steer clear of explicit party politics). Humour or a more sober tone? Confrontational or unifying? The choice is yours. Formal training isn’t a must, but a desire to make your voice heard certainly is!",04 May 2026,2026-05-04,2026-09-23 07:58:04.012059+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_0607d3ccd703,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/e10000-transitional-justice-grant-fellowship/,https://afield.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=793163623749ff92bce4091cd&id=8944611f3e&e=787e6c9df5,"AFIELD, Arts of the Working Class, and Framer Framed",en,"€10,000 Transitional Justice Grant & Fellowship","Applicants must be: Legal residents (including refugees/asylum seekers) in an EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country. Part of an initiative operationally active for at least two years. Using artistic methodologies as the central component of their work. Available for all fellowship components, including the residency and online thematic meetings.","€10,000 Transitional Justice Grant & Fellowship","Applicants must be: Legal residents (including refugees/asylum seekers) in an EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country. Part of an initiative operationally active for at least two years. Using artistic methodologies as the central component of their work. Available for all fellowship components, including the residency and online thematic meetings.",02 May 2026,2026-05-02,2026-09-23 07:58:04.016029+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_bf616e30e784,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/2026-visureal%c2%b7international-image-art-festival-viiaf-call-for-artists-and-art-organizations-worldwide/,https://viiaf.com/call-for-submissions/,VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF),en,2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF): Call for Artists and Art Organizations Worldwide,"The 2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF) invites submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide. VIIAF 2026 welcomes a wide range of image-based works, including photography, video art, short films, animation, interactive media, AI-generated imagery, and AR/VR installations.",2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF): Call for Artists and Art Organizations Worldwide,"The 2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF) invites submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide. VIIAF 2026 welcomes a wide range of image-based works, including photography, video art, short films, animation, interactive media, AI-generated imagery, and AR/VR installations.",01 May 2026,2026-05-01,2026-09-23 07:58:04.019189+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_cb1c6c5c2505,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/vila-31-x-art-explora-residency-programme-2027-sessions/,https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6107fc8664b5410e82635537/69ce6faf843161c681181739_Vila%2031%20x%20Art%20Explora_2027%20Open%20Call%202.pdf,"Vila 31, Art Explora Residency",en,"Vila 31 x Art Explora Residency Programme, 2027 Sessions","This residency program is open to artists and artist collectives, researchers, curators, and writers of all nationalities, without age restrictions , who can demonstrate a minimum of five years of professional activity and have exhibited their works and research at a national/international level.

Residency Programmes Three residency programmes are available: SOLO programme: open to artists and writers working across visual arts, performance, digital practices, literary works, or other experimental disciplines. COLLECTIVE Programme: open to collectives or duos of artists, researchers, curators, and writers working collaboratively on interdisciplinary, experimental, or research-based projects. If you are interested in the COLLECTIVE programme, only one application should be submitted by one of the collective members. For this programme, only one studio-apartment is provided, designed to accommodate collaborative work. The studio can host 2 residents ( shared bed ). If separate sleeping arrangements are required, two accommodation spaces will be provided.","Vila 31 x Art Explora Residency Programme, 2027 Sessions","This residency program is open to artists and artist collectives, researchers, curators, and writers of all nationalities, without age restrictions , who can demonstrate a minimum of five years of professional activity and have exhibited their works and research at a national/international level.

Residency Programmes Three residency programmes are available: SOLO programme: open to artists and writers working across visual arts, performance, digital practices, literary works, or other experimental disciplines. COLLECTIVE Programme: open to collectives or duos of artists, researchers, curators, and writers working collaboratively on interdisciplinary, experimental, or research-based projects. If you are interested in the COLLECTIVE programme, only one application should be submitted by one of the collective members. For this programme, only one studio-apartment is provided, designed to accommodate collaborative work. The studio can host 2 residents ( shared bed ). If separate sleeping arrangements are required, two accommodation spaces will be provided.",01 May 2026,2026-05-01,2026-09-23 07:58:04.021909+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_ea080b73ff61,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-illustrate-a-flag-for-potloodvenster/,,Potloodvenster,en,Open Call: Illustrate a Flag for Potloodvenster,Only 12 designers will be onboarded to design a 1 x 1.5 meter flag.,Open Call: Illustrate a Flag for Potloodvenster,Only 12 designers will be onboarded to design a 1 x 1.5 meter flag.,01 May 2026,2026-05-01,2026-09-23 07:58:04.025208+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_e9cea19ce978,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-individual-mobility-2025-2026/,https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-for-individual-mobility-2025-2026,Culture Moves Europe,en,Call for individual mobility 2025-2026,"Who can apply? Artists and cultural professionals, who are: legally residing in one of the Creative Europe countries, including the overseas countries and territories and outermost regions 18 years of age or older active in one of the following sectors: architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts; No specific level of experience is required The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.

What is required to apply? One project One artistic or cultural project to be carried out in another Creative Europe country, with the support of an international partner. This project must follow 2 of the following objectives: to learn, to create, to explore, or to connect. One international partner The international partner collaborates with the artists and cultural professionals during the project implementation. Applicants chose their own international partners, which can be an individual or an organisation. Supporting documents Applicants must upload the required supporting documents: official national identification proof of legal residence short curriculum vitae (CV) artistic and creative portfolio letter of invitation from the international partner",Call for individual mobility 2025-2026,"Who can apply? Artists and cultural professionals, who are: legally residing in one of the Creative Europe countries, including the overseas countries and territories and outermost regions 18 years of age or older active in one of the following sectors: architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts; No specific level of experience is required The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.

What is required to apply? One project One artistic or cultural project to be carried out in another Creative Europe country, with the support of an international partner. This project must follow 2 of the following objectives: to learn, to create, to explore, or to connect. One international partner The international partner collaborates with the artists and cultural professionals during the project implementation. Applicants chose their own international partners, which can be an individual or an organisation. Supporting documents Applicants must upload the required supporting documents: official national identification proof of legal residence short curriculum vitae (CV) artistic and creative portfolio letter of invitation from the international partner",30 Apr 2026,2026-04-30,2026-09-23 07:58:04.028570+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_4aedc4760cc0,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-zoop-connections-ii-kunstfort-vijfhuizen-czech-centre-brussels-call-for-artist-in-residence-2026/,https://www.kunstfort.nl/en/news/open-call-kunstfort-vijfhuizen-x-czech-centre-brussels/,"Czech Centre Brussels, Kunstfort Vijfhuizen, EUNIC Netherlands, Zoöp, and DutchCulture",en,Open Call Zoöp Connections II: Kunstfort Vijfhuizen & Czech Centre Brussels Call for Artist-in-Residence 2026,"Creative professionals and artists aged 18+, based in a Creative Europe country outside the Netherlands, with a demonstrable connection to Czech culture. Residents may come from a wide range of creative fields, including visual arts, design, research, literature, performance, music, technology, or other interdisciplinary practices.",Open Call Zoöp Connections II: Kunstfort Vijfhuizen & Czech Centre Brussels Call for Artist-in-Residence 2026,"Creative professionals and artists aged 18+, based in a Creative Europe country outside the Netherlands, with a demonstrable connection to Czech culture. Residents may come from a wide range of creative fields, including visual arts, design, research, literature, performance, music, technology, or other interdisciplinary practices.","April 30, 2026 (23:59 CET)",2026-04-30,2026-09-23 07:58:04.036086+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_b2bef0511012,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-residencies/,https://www.imal.org/en/events/appel-a-residences-ipo-2026-extra,iMAL,en,Open call for residencies,"The call is open to emerging artists engaged in a professional practice. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works. Candidates must reside in France or Belgium. There are two ways to apply: Option 1: Duos to be formed • Artists apply individually to the call without having a predefined partner. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates, then shared via Google Drive with all candidates on May 4. • This stage will allow artists to review applications and connect with other candidates to explore the possibility of collaborating on a joint project. Candidates will have from May 4 to May 22 to engage in these exchanges. • The pairs formed will be invited to complete a second questionnaire by May 22, with the name of their partner and a letter of intent regarding their co-creation project. Option 2: Existing duos • It is possible to apply directly with another artist for a co-creation project. The only prerequisite is that one artist must reside in France and the other in Belgium. Both artists are invited to respond individually to the call for applications, specifying that they are working on a joint project and providing the name of the artist they’re partnering with. • Please note: Existing duos should only answer the first application form, which closes on April 24. They must therefore submit their letter of intent detailing their joint project using this form. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates.",Open call for residencies,"The call is open to emerging artists engaged in a professional practice. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works. Candidates must reside in France or Belgium. There are two ways to apply: Option 1: Duos to be formed • Artists apply individually to the call without having a predefined partner. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates, then shared via Google Drive with all candidates on May 4. • This stage will allow artists to review applications and connect with other candidates to explore the possibility of collaborating on a joint project. Candidates will have from May 4 to May 22 to engage in these exchanges. • The pairs formed will be invited to complete a second questionnaire by May 22, with the name of their partner and a letter of intent regarding their co-creation project. Option 2: Existing duos • It is possible to apply directly with another artist for a co-creation project. The only prerequisite is that one artist must reside in France and the other in Belgium. Both artists are invited to respond individually to the call for applications, specifying that they are working on a joint project and providing the name of the artist they’re partnering with. • Please note: Existing duos should only answer the first application form, which closes on April 24. They must therefore submit their letter of intent detailing their joint project using this form. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates.",24 Apr 2026,2026-04-24,2026-09-23 07:58:04.039570+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a97a4eca3212,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-international-fikva-award-for-painters-2026/,https://fikva.art/submission-form/,FiKVA Foundation,en,OPEN CALL – International FIKVA Award for painters 2026,"The International FiKVA Award for painters is open to all artists 18 years of age or older. The FiKVA Award is open to all styles of representational painting – modern and classical realism, imaginative realism, hyperrealism, photorealism, luminism, surrealism etc – as long as the artwork reads as representational and not stylized or abstract. If your work captures the essence of the real world while reflecting your unique artistic voice, we want to see it!

ARTIST ELIGIBILITY
The FiKVA Award is open to all painters aged 18 and older, from anywhere in the world.

ARTWORK ELIGIBILITY
The work must be the artist’s original creation, produced solely by the artist, with copyrights exclusively owned by the artist. The work may be signed and may have participated in previous competitions. The work may be sold, provided the copyright of its image remains solely with the artist. Works must have been produced between 2024 and 2026. Works must be available for inclusion in an online exhibition. Works do not need to be available for sale.

ACCEPTED MEDIA
Oil, water-soluble oil paint, acrylic paint, watercolor, ink, gouache, tempera, and all traditional wet mediums on any support – canvas, board, paper, wood, panel, wall, aluminium, glass, etc. All works must be handmade; digital or mechanical works will not be considered.",OPEN CALL – International FIKVA Award for painters 2026,"The International FiKVA Award for painters is open to all artists 18 years of age or older. The FiKVA Award is open to all styles of representational painting – modern and classical realism, imaginative realism, hyperrealism, photorealism, luminism, surrealism etc – as long as the artwork reads as representational and not stylized or abstract. If your work captures the essence of the real world while reflecting your unique artistic voice, we want to see it!

ARTIST ELIGIBILITY
The FiKVA Award is open to all painters aged 18 and older, from anywhere in the world.

ARTWORK ELIGIBILITY
The work must be the artist’s original creation, produced solely by the artist, with copyrights exclusively owned by the artist. The work may be signed and may have participated in previous competitions. The work may be sold, provided the copyright of its image remains solely with the artist. Works must have been produced between 2024 and 2026. Works must be available for inclusion in an online exhibition. Works do not need to be available for sale.

ACCEPTED MEDIA
Oil, water-soluble oil paint, acrylic paint, watercolor, ink, gouache, tempera, and all traditional wet mediums on any support – canvas, board, paper, wood, panel, wall, aluminium, glass, etc. All works must be handmade; digital or mechanical works will not be considered.","22 April 2026, 12:00 noon (Brussels time).",2027-04-22,2026-09-23 07:58:04.088752+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_5d9b2594f95d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/fellowship-programma-call-2026/,https://framaforms.org/imal-fellowship-programme-2026-1770642755,"iMAL, Cloud Seven",en,Fellowship programme: call 2026,"This programme is specifically designed for professional artists who wish to shift or deepen their practice through technology. We are looking for candidates who:
Have a solid background in contemporary art but limited experience with digital tools. Artists that while rooted in contemporary art, demonstrate an initial exploration of technological tools and show a strong interest in deepening this approach through a committed project requiring curatorial and technical support within iMAL. View this residency as a learning opportunity rather than a standard production slot. Are seeking curatorial mentorship and technical guidance to explore new territories.
Note: Artists with extensive experience in digital arts may be considered overqualified, as the programme’s primary goal is to provide a space for growth, experimentation, and the acquisition of new technical and critical skills.",Fellowship programme: call 2026,"This programme is specifically designed for professional artists who wish to shift or deepen their practice through technology. We are looking for candidates who:
Have a solid background in contemporary art but limited experience with digital tools. Artists that while rooted in contemporary art, demonstrate an initial exploration of technological tools and show a strong interest in deepening this approach through a committed project requiring curatorial and technical support within iMAL. View this residency as a learning opportunity rather than a standard production slot. Are seeking curatorial mentorship and technical guidance to explore new territories.
Note: Artists with extensive experience in digital arts may be considered overqualified, as the programme’s primary goal is to provide a space for growth, experimentation, and the acquisition of new technical and critical skills.","April 19, 2026",2026-04-19,2026-09-23 07:58:04.091930+00:00
