kunsten_be_flanders_dd391ca69243,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/courants-du-monde-individual-short-term-program/,https://www.culture.gouv.fr/catalogue-des-demarches-et-subventions/appels-a-projets-candidatures/courants-du-monde-sejour-culture-2026,Ministère de la culture France,en,Courants du monde individual short-term program,"French-speaking or English-speaking foreign cultural professionals working in national, regional, or local cultural administrations, institutions, and organizations across all cultural sectors.

Eligibility criteria
This international program welcomes experienced cultural professionals from around the world who are actively engaged in cultural projects within their home countries. These professionals must be engaged, or about to engage, in a cultural project with French partners. However to achieve this, they need to develop their knowledge of, and contacts within, the French cultural sector.

Ineligibility criteria
The program is not open to artists, students, teachers, researchers, of representatives of the French cultural network abroad (Cooperation and Cultural Action Services of the French Embassy, Alliances françaises, Instituts Français) who may benefit from other programs.",Courants du monde individual short-term program,"French-speaking or English-speaking foreign cultural professionals working in national, regional, or local cultural administrations, institutions, and organizations across all cultural sectors.

Eligibility criteria
This international program welcomes experienced cultural professionals from around the world who are actively engaged in cultural projects within their home countries. These professionals must be engaged, or about to engage, in a cultural project with French partners. However to achieve this, they need to develop their knowledge of, and contacts within, the French cultural sector.

Ineligibility criteria
The program is not open to artists, students, teachers, researchers, of representatives of the French cultural network abroad (Cooperation and Cultural Action Services of the French Embassy, Alliances françaises, Instituts Français) who may benefit from other programs.",15 Mar 2026,2026-03-15,2026-09-23 07:58:04.135496+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2c5ed7b40a1d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/european-media-art-platform-residency-programme-2026/,,European Media Art Platform (EMAP),en,European Media Art Platform Residency Programme 2026,"EMAP invites artists, artist duos, collectives, and artistic collaborations working in digital, media, robotic, and bio art to apply for a two-month production residency in 2026. The EMAP residency programme places a strong emphasis on collaboration. Applicants must therefore apply as a duo or collective, or propose a collaborative project with a partner of their choice or with a collaborator local to the host institution. Artists apply to the EMAP consortium as a whole and indicate their preferred host organisations in order of priority: Ars Electronica, Linz, Austria Chroniques, Marseille, France CIKE – Creative Industry Košice, Košice, Slovakia gnration, Braga, Portugal iMAL, Brussels, Belgium IMPAKT [Centre for Media Culture], Utrecht, The Netherlands Kersnikova Institute (Kapelica Gallery), Ljubljana, Slovenia KONTEJNER | Bureau of Contemporary Art Praxis, Zagreb, Croatia LABoral Centro de Arte y Creación Industrial, Gijón, Spain (only possible between September and November in 2026) MEET Digital Culture Center, Milan, Italy NeMe, Limassol, Cyprus Onassis Stegi, Athens, Greece RIXC Centre for New Media Culture, Riga, Latvia werkleitz – Centre for Media Art, Halle (Saale), Germany WRO Art Center, Wrocław, Poland Applicants must be EU residents or taxpayers in an EU member state, or residents/taxpayers of one of the eligible non-EU countries. Undergraduate and Master’s students are not eligible. PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.",European Media Art Platform Residency Programme 2026,"EMAP invites artists, artist duos, collectives, and artistic collaborations working in digital, media, robotic, and bio art to apply for a two-month production residency in 2026. The EMAP residency programme places a strong emphasis on collaboration. Applicants must therefore apply as a duo or collective, or propose a collaborative project with a partner of their choice or with a collaborator local to the host institution. Artists apply to the EMAP consortium as a whole and indicate their preferred host organisations in order of priority: Ars Electronica, Linz, Austria Chroniques, Marseille, France CIKE – Creative Industry Košice, Košice, Slovakia gnration, Braga, Portugal iMAL, Brussels, Belgium IMPAKT [Centre for Media Culture], Utrecht, The Netherlands Kersnikova Institute (Kapelica Gallery), Ljubljana, Slovenia KONTEJNER | Bureau of Contemporary Art Praxis, Zagreb, Croatia LABoral Centro de Arte y Creación Industrial, Gijón, Spain (only possible between September and November in 2026) MEET Digital Culture Center, Milan, Italy NeMe, Limassol, Cyprus Onassis Stegi, Athens, Greece RIXC Centre for New Media Culture, Riga, Latvia werkleitz – Centre for Media Art, Halle (Saale), Germany WRO Art Center, Wrocław, Poland Applicants must be EU residents or taxpayers in an EU member state, or residents/taxpayers of one of the eligible non-EU countries. Undergraduate and Master’s students are not eligible. PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.",13 Mar 2026,2026-03-13,2026-09-23 07:58:04.138545+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_28881ec0704a,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ape-camp-2026-open-call-for-overseas-artists-producers-and-engineers/,,Arts Council Korea,en,"APE CAMP 2026: Open call for overseas artists, producers and engineers","Participation requirements General (mandatory) Applications must be submitted by individuals only. This open call is for international participants who do not hold Korean nationality. Participants must be able to attend all programs during the camp period from 12 to 16 June 2026. (※ Selection will be cancelled if a participant withdraws after selection or attends only part of the program.) Applicants must be able to communicate in English. Art category (Mandatory) Young artists and producers aged 39 or under who are actively engaged in creative practices related to art–technology convergence Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc. Technology category (Mandatory) Professionals, researchers, and experts in technology fields who possess specialised knowledge applicable to art–technology convergence–based creative practices. The eligible technology fields include, but are not limited to, the areas listed below. Applicants working in other relevant technology fields not listed may also apply. Stage Technologies: Stage lighting, stage sound, stage equipment, stage video, immersive sound, kinetic art, etc. Emerging Technologies: Artificial intelligence (AI), blockchain, data science and technologies, development (e.g. web, mobile applications, games), metaverse, motion capture, robotics, VR/AR/XR, etc. Core Sciences: Biotechnology, chemistry, geology, life sciences, neuroscience, physics, etc. Applied Engineering: Advanced materials, aerospace engineering, batteries, energy, Internet of Things (IoT), mobility, nanotechnology, new materials engineering, quantum computing, wearable technology, etc. (Note) Preference will be given to early-career technology professionals.","APE CAMP 2026: Open call for overseas artists, producers and engineers","Participation requirements General (mandatory) Applications must be submitted by individuals only. This open call is for international participants who do not hold Korean nationality. Participants must be able to attend all programs during the camp period from 12 to 16 June 2026. (※ Selection will be cancelled if a participant withdraws after selection or attends only part of the program.) Applicants must be able to communicate in English. Art category (Mandatory) Young artists and producers aged 39 or under who are actively engaged in creative practices related to art–technology convergence Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc. Technology category (Mandatory) Professionals, researchers, and experts in technology fields who possess specialised knowledge applicable to art–technology convergence–based creative practices. The eligible technology fields include, but are not limited to, the areas listed below. Applicants working in other relevant technology fields not listed may also apply. Stage Technologies: Stage lighting, stage sound, stage equipment, stage video, immersive sound, kinetic art, etc. Emerging Technologies: Artificial intelligence (AI), blockchain, data science and technologies, development (e.g. web, mobile applications, games), metaverse, motion capture, robotics, VR/AR/XR, etc. Core Sciences: Biotechnology, chemistry, geology, life sciences, neuroscience, physics, etc. Applied Engineering: Advanced materials, aerospace engineering, batteries, energy, Internet of Things (IoT), mobility, nanotechnology, new materials engineering, quantum computing, wearable technology, etc. (Note) Preference will be given to early-career technology professionals.","Thursday, 12 March 2026, 23:59 KST",2026-03-12,2026-09-23 07:58:04.146738+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_8a344b3ec711,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ga-met-kunstenpunt-naar-classicalnext-in-budapest/,,Flanders Arts Institute & WBM,en,Join Flanders Arts Institute at Classical:NEXT in Budapest,"Want to join Flanders Arts Institute?

Financial support from Flanders Arts Institute:

