€ 200 per registered person for those receiving an operating subsidy of less than €150000

Are you eligible for this extra financial support? If so, please contact Ward Bosmans after you registered.",08 Mar 2026,2026-03-08,2026-09-23 07:58:04.150004+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_78c404ddf0fa,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-par-hasard-2/,,Par Hasard,en,Open Call Par Hasard,For who – You have a degree in the arts or relevant experience in the arts sector – you share a work-in-progress or an experiment (max 15min) – your work is suitable for the location (limited technical resources) – your work-in-progress should have a performative character,Open Call Par Hasard,For who – You have a degree in the arts or relevant experience in the arts sector – you share a work-in-progress or an experiment (max 15min) – your work is suitable for the location (limited technical resources) – your work-in-progress should have a performative character,"The open call will close on the 6 th of March, at 11:59 pm.",2027-03-06,2026-09-23 07:58:04.154568+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_7dee819ffe18,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-the-breadwinner-registry-a-kinship-accord-by-shif-t/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdL85-EM8OoIAPzfV4lWriMLIpgUWZUqzPj7GbSkrlbpreRBA/viewform,Shif—t*,en,Open Call: The Breadwinner Registry – A Kinship Accord by Shif—t*,"We are looking for artists, cultural workers, thinkers, organisers, designers, producers, scenographers, writers, educators, and hybrid practitioners who:
Want to build and maintain community
Value long term relationships over quick wins or transactional interactions;
Invest time in trust building, shared rituals, and collective memory;
Show up consistently, especially when things are messy or uncertain;
Create spaces where people feel seen, heard, and able to contribute;
Understand that community is not a product to launch but a garden to tend;
Are interested in working collectively rather than competitively
Share knowledge, resources, and opportunities openly;
Celebrate others’ progress as fuel for the whole group;
Approach challenges with “how can we?” instead of “who wins?”;
Make decisions collaboratively when possible, with transparency and care;
See collaboration as a multiplier that expands what is possible for everyone;
Are open to experimentation, conversation and mutual support
Treat ideas as prototypes rather than polished monuments;
Welcome dialogue, disagreement, and evolution of thought;
Offer and receive feedback as a form of care;
Embrace uncertainty as a creative laboratory rather than a threat;
Step in to support others, and allow yourself to be supported in return;
Want to be part of a growing network rather than a fixed project
Prefer ecosystems over rigid structures;
Invite new people, perspectives, and partnerships over time;
Allow the direction of the work to evolve organically;
Stay flexible about roles, leadership, and contributions;
See the network as a living organism that expands, adapts, and renews itself;
to enter a mutual platforming agreement with the collective.",Open Call: The Breadwinner Registry – A Kinship Accord by Shif—t*,"We are looking for artists, cultural workers, thinkers, organisers, designers, producers, scenographers, writers, educators, and hybrid practitioners who:
Want to build and maintain community
Value long term relationships over quick wins or transactional interactions;
Invest time in trust building, shared rituals, and collective memory;
Show up consistently, especially when things are messy or uncertain;
Create spaces where people feel seen, heard, and able to contribute;
Understand that community is not a product to launch but a garden to tend;
Are interested in working collectively rather than competitively
Share knowledge, resources, and opportunities openly;
Celebrate others’ progress as fuel for the whole group;
Approach challenges with “how can we?” instead of “who wins?”;
Make decisions collaboratively when possible, with transparency and care;
See collaboration as a multiplier that expands what is possible for everyone;
Are open to experimentation, conversation and mutual support
Treat ideas as prototypes rather than polished monuments;
Welcome dialogue, disagreement, and evolution of thought;
Offer and receive feedback as a form of care;
Embrace uncertainty as a creative laboratory rather than a threat;
Step in to support others, and allow yourself to be supported in return;
Want to be part of a growing network rather than a fixed project
Prefer ecosystems over rigid structures;
Invite new people, perspectives, and partnerships over time;
Allow the direction of the work to evolve organically;
Stay flexible about roles, leadership, and contributions;
See the network as a living organism that expands, adapts, and renews itself;
to enter a mutual platforming agreement with the collective.",06 Mar 2026,2026-03-06,2026-09-23 07:58:04.157896+00:00
