kunsten_be_flanders_4d23f5817f2e,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-oproep-unesco-aschberg-voor-projecten-rond-artistieke-vrijheid/,https://www.unesco.org/creativity/en/articles/call-projects-unesco-aschberg-programme-artists-and-cultural-professionals-0,UNESCO,en,Call for projects “UNESCO-Aschberg Programme for Artists and Cultural Professionals”,"The United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO) launches a call open to governments and public institutions, as well as civil society organizations, to support initiatives aimed at protecting and promoting the status of the artist and artistic freedom.",Call for projects “UNESCO-Aschberg Programme for Artists and Cultural Professionals”,"The United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO) launches a call open to governments and public institutions, as well as civil society organizations, to support initiatives aimed at protecting and promoting the status of the artist and artistic freedom.",23 Feb 2026,2026-02-23,2026-09-23 07:58:04.180339+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_66619beb67ef,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/helsinki-international-curatorial-programme-hicp/,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/helsinki-international-curatorial-programme-hicp/,HIAP – Helsinki International Artist Programme,en,Helsinki International Curatorial Programme (HICP),Who can apply: Curators based outside Finland with 2–3+ years professional curatorial experience (institutional or independent).,Helsinki International Curatorial Programme (HICP),Who can apply: Curators based outside Finland with 2–3+ years professional curatorial experience (institutional or independent).,"Mon 23 Feb 2026, 15:00 (GMT+2)",2026-02-23,2026-09-23 07:58:04.186901+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_7b3d4f68b4d8,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/auditions-conversations-new-xrperformance-by-paul-boereboom-leon-rogissart/,,Paul Boereboom & Leon Rogissart,en,Auditions Conversations – New XRPerformance by Paul Boereboom & Leon Rogissart,"We are looking for vocal performers who: _have a classical alt / baritone/tenor vocal range _are comfortable with live performance and embodied presence _enjoy participatory interaction with an audience _have affinity with music theatre, contemporary music, and/or ritual practices _enjoy collaborative, research-driven creation processes",Auditions Conversations – New XRPerformance by Paul Boereboom & Leon Rogissart,"We are looking for vocal performers who: _have a classical alt / baritone/tenor vocal range _are comfortable with live performance and embodied presence _enjoy participatory interaction with an audience _have affinity with music theatre, contemporary music, and/or ritual practices _enjoy collaborative, research-driven creation processes",23 Feb 2026,2026-02-23,2026-09-23 07:58:04.189989+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_399ae984ab54,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/printmaking-residency-milaan/,http://www.gate44.eu/open-call/,Gate 44,en,Printmaking residency (Milaan),"Artists whose practice already includes printmaking to some extent. Artists who have a minimum base knowledge and understanding of one or more print techniques (even though professional technical assistance will be provided). Artists who are eager to expand their technical tool-kit and expressive potential. Artists who embrace experimentation, interdisciplinary approaches, and the blending of multiple printmaking methods.

Must be able to travel to Milan for the scheduled residency, and be able to use the provided materials and equipment. Uphold a professional work ethic and conduct throughout the residency. Work must fit within a maximum paper size of 50 × 70 cm (no minimum size). A minimum production of 10 finished prints is required. Create a minimum of one printed edition or multiple unique pieces. Agree to provide n. 3 (three) copies of each edition printed to Gate44’s archives.",Printmaking residency (Milaan),"Artists whose practice already includes printmaking to some extent. Artists who have a minimum base knowledge and understanding of one or more print techniques (even though professional technical assistance will be provided). Artists who are eager to expand their technical tool-kit and expressive potential. Artists who embrace experimentation, interdisciplinary approaches, and the blending of multiple printmaking methods.

Must be able to travel to Milan for the scheduled residency, and be able to use the provided materials and equipment. Uphold a professional work ethic and conduct throughout the residency. Work must fit within a maximum paper size of 50 × 70 cm (no minimum size). A minimum production of 10 finished prints is required. Create a minimum of one printed edition or multiple unique pieces. Agree to provide n. 3 (three) copies of each edition printed to Gate44’s archives.",22 February 2026,2026-02-22,2026-09-23 07:58:04.193401+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_3239893e64df,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-curatorial-fellow-public-outreach-community-engagement/,http://actiris.brussels/nl/burgers/beroepsinlevingsstage/,Kunsthal Mechelen and the Curatorial Studies programme at KASK & Conservatorium,en,Open Call: Curatorial Fellow – Public Outreach & Community Engagement,"We are looking for someone who: Has a background in curatorial practice, museum studies, or arts education. Can combine conceptual thinking with practical programme design. Is enthusiastic about community engagement and building volunteer networks. Enjoys experimenting with formats for children, families, and multigenerational audiences. Values collaboration and can work across departments to integrate public-facing activities into the curatorial vision. Can support the team with research of accessibility / public outreach related grants. Has strong communicative and writing skills in English and Dutch.",Open Call: Curatorial Fellow – Public Outreach & Community Engagement,"We are looking for someone who: Has a background in curatorial practice, museum studies, or arts education. Can combine conceptual thinking with practical programme design. Is enthusiastic about community engagement and building volunteer networks. Enjoys experimenting with formats for children, families, and multigenerational audiences. Values collaboration and can work across departments to integrate public-facing activities into the curatorial vision. Can support the team with research of accessibility / public outreach related grants. Has strong communicative and writing skills in English and Dutch.","February 22nd 2026 , midnight.",2026-02-22,2026-09-23 07:58:04.200190+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_fbadd44e7fb1,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-submissions-file-electronic-language-international-festival/,https://file.org.br/highlight/file-2026-inscricoes-abertas-para-festival-de-arte-e-tecnologia/,FILE – International Electronic Language Festival,en,Call for submissions: FILE – Electronic Language International Festival,"FILE invites Brazilian and international artists , as well as researchers, educators, and creators , to submit original artistic works and educational proposals — lectures, workshops, and training activities — focused on contemporary technological poetics.",Call for submissions: FILE – Electronic Language International Festival,"FILE invites Brazilian and international artists , as well as researchers, educators, and creators , to submit original artistic works and educational proposals — lectures, workshops, and training activities — focused on contemporary technological poetics.",19 Feb 2026,2026-02-19,2026-09-23 07:58:04.204026+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_d04919f3f6f8,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-code-2026-reclaiming-digital-agency/,https://tally.so/r/9q90a4,IMPAKT [Centre for Media Culture],en,Open call: CODE 2026 – Reclaiming Digital Agency,"Are you an artist, designer, researcher, software designer or developer? Working in marketing, law, technology, policymaking, politics? Interested in human rights and equality? Are you open to working on collaborative projects that can speak to the imagination of a wider audience and inspire them to think about their digital agency? If you answered yes to any of these questions, or if you’re simply concerned about our digital rights and the lack of agency across the online platforms we use, then IMPAKT is looking for you!

With the open call for CODE 2026, we invite creatives, professional and non-professional artists, and concerned citizens of the Netherlands and Belgium to embark on a journey of critical discourse and collaborative creation regarding digital rights.",Open call: CODE 2026 – Reclaiming Digital Agency,"Are you an artist, designer, researcher, software designer or developer? Working in marketing, law, technology, policymaking, politics? Interested in human rights and equality? Are you open to working on collaborative projects that can speak to the imagination of a wider audience and inspire them to think about their digital agency? If you answered yes to any of these questions, or if you’re simply concerned about our digital rights and the lack of agency across the online platforms we use, then IMPAKT is looking for you!

With the open call for CODE 2026, we invite creatives, professional and non-professional artists, and concerned citizens of the Netherlands and Belgium to embark on a journey of critical discourse and collaborative creation regarding digital rights.",15 Feb 2026,2026-02-15,2026-09-23 07:58:04.208183+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_0f461816d18d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-performers-and-understudies/,,Kunsten,en,Call for performers and understudies,"We’re looking for three different profiles for Frames (one replacement and two understudies). If you want to audition for one of these roles, please have a look at the in depth specifications. 1 – Replacement (who will take over performances starting from summer 2026) Strong skills and experience in partner acrobatics Big range of mobility and strength comfortable with hanging Strong base profile Squat flexibility Height between 175 and 195 cm Maximum weight of 80 kg → more specifications 2 – Understudy/base profile (who can jump in, in case of injury/double booking) Comfortable as an aerial and floor base Height between 180 – 195 cm Maximum weight of 85 kg Strong skills and experience in partner acrobatics Comfortable with hanging at a height of 4,5 m Big range of mobility and strength → more specifications 3 – Understudy/flyer profile (who can jump in, in case of injury/double booking) Flexibility, strength and strong handstand skills are required Height between 150 – 175 cm Maximum weight of 65 kg Strong skills and experience in partner acrobatics Comfortable with hanging at a height of 4,5 m Big range of mobility and strength → more specifications",Call for performers and understudies,"We’re looking for three different profiles for Frames (one replacement and two understudies). If you want to audition for one of these roles, please have a look at the in depth specifications. 1 – Replacement (who will take over performances starting from summer 2026) Strong skills and experience in partner acrobatics Big range of mobility and strength comfortable with hanging Strong base profile Squat flexibility Height between 175 and 195 cm Maximum weight of 80 kg → more specifications 2 – Understudy/base profile (who can jump in, in case of injury/double booking) Comfortable as an aerial and floor base Height between 180 – 195 cm Maximum weight of 85 kg Strong skills and experience in partner acrobatics Comfortable with hanging at a height of 4,5 m Big range of mobility and strength → more specifications 3 – Understudy/flyer profile (who can jump in, in case of injury/double booking) Flexibility, strength and strong handstand skills are required Height between 150 – 175 cm Maximum weight of 65 kg Strong skills and experience in partner acrobatics Comfortable with hanging at a height of 4,5 m Big range of mobility and strength → more specifications",14 Feb 2026,2026-02-14,2026-09-23 07:58:04.211644+00:00
