kunsten_be_flanders_ab2801ef4c6f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-word-artist-in-residence-bij-muziekhuis-rataplan-2026/,https://www.cognitoforms.com/Rataplan1/ArtistInResidenceRataplanOpenCall2026,Rataplan,en,Open call: Become Artist in Residence at music venue Rataplan,"Who can apply? Up-and-coming, musical, professional talent with a unique approach to jazz. Also mid-career artists who collaborate across generations on a surprising and adventurous project that enriches the jazz scene. Musicians or collectives with projects that meet the following criteria: Your practice is based on jazz and can be enhanced by other art forms. These can be other music genres, encounters with performance (theatre, slam poetry, dance, etc.), visual/audiovisual art. Proposals aimed at a young audience are also eligible. You are an emerging, professional and adventurous musician with a determined outlook on the future. Or you have been active for some time and are working on an innovative project. You pay attention to a variety of sounds and representation in your band. The residency focuses on artistic development. It is not part of an academic research study, the completion of an album or rehearsals for a release. You will be part of the Rataplan breeding ground: you will engage in dialogue with the other residents, share expertise and be present during other performances. You are interested and open to collaboration with Rataplan. This is an additional commitment that you take on as an artist in residence. You have an affinity with jazz in connection with the metropolitan context. Your music reflects the urban soundscape.",Open call: Become Artist in Residence at music venue Rataplan,"Who can apply? Up-and-coming, musical, professional talent with a unique approach to jazz. Also mid-career artists who collaborate across generations on a surprising and adventurous project that enriches the jazz scene. Musicians or collectives with projects that meet the following criteria: Your practice is based on jazz and can be enhanced by other art forms. These can be other music genres, encounters with performance (theatre, slam poetry, dance, etc.), visual/audiovisual art. Proposals aimed at a young audience are also eligible. You are an emerging, professional and adventurous musician with a determined outlook on the future. Or you have been active for some time and are working on an innovative project. You pay attention to a variety of sounds and representation in your band. The residency focuses on artistic development. It is not part of an academic research study, the completion of an album or rehearsals for a release. You will be part of the Rataplan breeding ground: you will engage in dialogue with the other residents, share expertise and be present during other performances. You are interested and open to collaboration with Rataplan. This is an additional commitment that you take on as an artist in residence. You have an affinity with jazz in connection with the metropolitan context. Your music reflects the urban soundscape.",18 January 2026,2026-01-18,2026-09-23 07:58:04.237308+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_d3e08cdf7f83,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-bosacademie/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfb0m1HNOgYbbnOPtUSi0ZbJGfIq5NKnmB59KM9muyr7GFYKQ/viewform,Het Bos,en,Open Call Bosacademie,"Criteria: You are between 18 and 28 years old. You live in Belgium and/or independently reach Het Bos (Ankerrui 5/7, Antwerp) Your project includes a public performance as a closing or interim presentation Your project aligns with Het Bos’s mission. You actively participate in the Boscademie project. We meet an average of 7 times a year. Project proposals are selected based on feasibility, necessity, focus, and relevance, among other factors. We appreciate it if you involve one or more communities in your project.",Open Call Bosacademie,"Criteria: You are between 18 and 28 years old. You live in Belgium and/or independently reach Het Bos (Ankerrui 5/7, Antwerp) Your project includes a public performance as a closing or interim presentation Your project aligns with Het Bos’s mission. You actively participate in the Boscademie project. We meet an average of 7 times a year. Project proposals are selected based on feasibility, necessity, focus, and relevance, among other factors. We appreciate it if you involve one or more communities in your project.",14 Jan 2026,2026-01-14,2026-09-23 07:58:04.242184+00:00
