kunsten_be_flanders_77d04e963291,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/dingen-die-niet-verkopen-verkopen-u-dingen/,https://www.dingendienietverkopen.be/calls,Dingen die niet verkopen,en,Open call Dingen die niet verkopen (‘Stuff that does not sell’),"We are looking for unique objects and/or editions/multiples that tell a false or distorted narrative through text or image. Three-dimensional works and objects, as well as zines and alternative forms of publication, are eligible. We prefer objects that can be displayed on a shelf, newspaper carousel, or table. Works intended for wall mounting are not eligible. Specifics: Your work tells a (fictional) story through text and/or image. We are looking for small works: you can hold them in one hand and they cost no more than €100 (including VAT). We do not take ownership of your work, and you receive the full amount as agreed upon if sold. We will add an additional 20% to the sales price to cover the costs and communication of this exhibition, which we keep. To ensure a smooth selection process, we ask for the title of the work, its dimensions, year of production, the price (including VAT), and a short description . If applicable, we would also like to know how many copies of the work are available Submit a maximum of three artworks by 11:59 PM on November 16th , along with a brief explanation and relevant links. Incomplete submissions will not be considered. If you are selected, you must ensure that your work arrives at Dingen die niet verkopen (Oude Beurs 62, 2000 Antwerp) during the weekend of December 5th. After the exhibition, you have to collect the works yourself, if they aren’t sold.",Open call Dingen die niet verkopen (‘Stuff that does not sell’),"We are looking for unique objects and/or editions/multiples that tell a false or distorted narrative through text or image. Three-dimensional works and objects, as well as zines and alternative forms of publication, are eligible. We prefer objects that can be displayed on a shelf, newspaper carousel, or table. Works intended for wall mounting are not eligible. Specifics: Your work tells a (fictional) story through text and/or image. We are looking for small works: you can hold them in one hand and they cost no more than €100 (including VAT). We do not take ownership of your work, and you receive the full amount as agreed upon if sold. We will add an additional 20% to the sales price to cover the costs and communication of this exhibition, which we keep. To ensure a smooth selection process, we ask for the title of the work, its dimensions, year of production, the price (including VAT), and a short description . If applicable, we would also like to know how many copies of the work are available Submit a maximum of three artworks by 11:59 PM on November 16th , along with a brief explanation and relevant links. Incomplete submissions will not be considered. If you are selected, you must ensure that your work arrives at Dingen die niet verkopen (Oude Beurs 62, 2000 Antwerp) during the weekend of December 5th. After the exhibition, you have to collect the works yourself, if they aren’t sold.",11:59 PM on November 16th,2026-11-16,2026-09-23 07:58:04.388829+00:00
