kunsten_be_flanders_4b574ff6fc82,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-2025-visible-mag-contemporary-art-essay-prize/,https://www.visible-mag.com/p/open-call-2025-contemporary-art-essay-prize,Visible Mag,en,Open Call – 2025 Visible Mag Contemporary Art Essay Prize,"In line with the Magazine’s experimental nature, we are happy to accept short essays that reference photography in any way for this year’s prize. The Essay Prize is a celebration of the diverse perspectives in the arts. You are welcome to address the topic of the Prize from any perspective, such as economic, financial, sociological, historical, political, anthropological, anecdotal, legal, conservation, critical, cultural, Science, Technology, and Society (STS), and transdisciplinary. The ideal essay for the Prize is around 500 – 1000 words, with no more than 1500 words all inclusive.",Open Call – 2025 Visible Mag Contemporary Art Essay Prize,"In line with the Magazine’s experimental nature, we are happy to accept short essays that reference photography in any way for this year’s prize. The Essay Prize is a celebration of the diverse perspectives in the arts. You are welcome to address the topic of the Prize from any perspective, such as economic, financial, sociological, historical, political, anthropological, anecdotal, legal, conservation, critical, cultural, Science, Technology, and Society (STS), and transdisciplinary. The ideal essay for the Prize is around 500 – 1000 words, with no more than 1500 words all inclusive.",31 Dec 2025,2025-12-31,2026-09-23 11:35:02.493361+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_b363b1956897,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/sofam-beurzen-2025-6/,,SOFAM,en,SOFAM Grants 2025/6,"The SOFAM grants are destined for professional visual artists in Belgium, who are a member of SOFAM or who plan to join. The funds that make these grants possible are allocated annually by SOFAM’s members. Are you already a member of another collective management society in Belgium for visual work? Then, unfortunately, this call is not for you. Do read the conditions on the next tab carefully to find out more about who is eligible to apply.

Support is important at every stage You can participate from the moment you have completed your art studies and are embarking on your artistic practice. You are also welcome to participate if you already have an established practice. If you picked up your practice again after a break, and you have produced a body of work you feel ready to share, you are also most welcome to apply. Quality prevails.

A celebration of practices, and an editorial balance We aim to award the grants to a variety of artistic visions. In doing so, we aim to include various artistic disciplines (photography, visual arts in all its forms, illustration…) but also differing life experiences that underpin the artistic proposals. We ask the jury to select different visual languages, whilst considering the balance of the whole. The strength of the images submitted is a key deciding factor.

A new element in this call A limited number of artists who apply but aren’t selected for a SOFAM 2025/6 grant may receive a SOFAM mini-grant worth €500. Eligibility requirements: the candidate must have been a member of SOFAM since at least July 1st 2025 selection by the jury",SOFAM Grants 2025/6,"The SOFAM grants are destined for professional visual artists in Belgium, who are a member of SOFAM or who plan to join. The funds that make these grants possible are allocated annually by SOFAM’s members. Are you already a member of another collective management society in Belgium for visual work? Then, unfortunately, this call is not for you. Do read the conditions on the next tab carefully to find out more about who is eligible to apply.

Support is important at every stage You can participate from the moment you have completed your art studies and are embarking on your artistic practice. You are also welcome to participate if you already have an established practice. If you picked up your practice again after a break, and you have produced a body of work you feel ready to share, you are also most welcome to apply. Quality prevails.

A celebration of practices, and an editorial balance We aim to award the grants to a variety of artistic visions. In doing so, we aim to include various artistic disciplines (photography, visual arts in all its forms, illustration…) but also differing life experiences that underpin the artistic proposals. We ask the jury to select different visual languages, whilst considering the balance of the whole. The strength of the images submitted is a key deciding factor.

A new element in this call A limited number of artists who apply but aren’t selected for a SOFAM 2025/6 grant may receive a SOFAM mini-grant worth €500. Eligibility requirements: the candidate must have been a member of SOFAM since at least July 1st 2025 selection by the jury",28 Dec 2025,2025-12-28,2026-09-23 11:35:02.499854+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_d4dcb3347320,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/imal-ipo-call-for-residencies-2026/,https://www.imal.org/en/events/ipo26,iMAL,en,iMAL iPO call for residencies 2026,"iMAL Project Office is an open call aimed at artists and creators based in Belgium. Through residencies of maximum one month at iMAL, we seek to provide production & research assistance to support and develop new artistic projects.",iMAL iPO call for residencies 2026,"iMAL Project Office is an open call aimed at artists and creators based in Belgium. Through residencies of maximum one month at iMAL, we seek to provide production & research assistance to support and develop new artistic projects.",22 Dec 2025,2025-12-22,2026-09-23 11:35:02.503465+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_e4a2cb6c28a5,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ga-op-residentie-bij-a-two-dogs-company-imal/,https://www.imal.org/en/events/ipo26/stages,iMAL and A Two Dogs Company,en,Open Call residency at A Two Dogs Company & iMAL,"This call is aimed at emerging artists. Applicants must be resident in Belgium, regardless of nationality, gender, religion or ethnic origin. They strongly encourage candidates of all origins and identities to apply. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works.",Open Call residency at A Two Dogs Company & iMAL,"This call is aimed at emerging artists. Applicants must be resident in Belgium, regardless of nationality, gender, religion or ethnic origin. They strongly encourage candidates of all origins and identities to apply. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works.",22 Dec 2025,2025-12-22,2026-09-23 11:35:02.507260+00:00
